{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XD1FArgnMbEr9vounfUsHi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — ec_hte_llm_annotation\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n5\t- Deadline: ARR submission May 25, 2026; commitment deadline August 2, 2026\n6\t- Format: Long paper, 8 pages + unlimited references\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条，可证伪)\n9\t\n10\t1. **Bias Mechanism Discovery**: When LLM misclassification rates for an effect modifier vary across subgroups, applying a global (pooled) correction to subgroup-level CATE estimates introduces systematic bias — over-correcting low-error subgroups and under-correcting high-error ones. In realistic settings, this \"debiasing\" can worsen CATE bias by 2-3x (median across configurations), with amplification up to 5.9x for K=4 subgroups; when naive bias is near zero, global correction creates bias where none existed. For the difference-in-means estimator, the amplification magnitude does NOT monotonically increase with K (K=2 extreme: up to 2.86× vs K=4 extreme: up to 2.41×); however, with nonlinear estimators such as CausalForest, more subgroups amplify the effect substantially (K=4/extreme: up to 5.9×) due to compounding estimation noise in tree-based CATE. Global correction increases subgroup-level bias in ~50% of the parameter space.\n11\t\n12\t2. **EC-HTE Solution**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified correction (EC-HTE) substantially reduces subgroup-level bias when misclassification heterogeneity is sufficiently high, while controlling estimation variance through partial pooling. HB provides meaningful RMSE reduction by borrowing strength across groups (classic James-Stein shrinkage). We provide precise crossover thresholds: EC-HTE outperforms global correction in RMSE with as few as 250 expert labels (K=2, high heterogeneity), scaling to ~1000 for K=4. **Boundary condition**: when expert labels per subgroup < ~25, shrinkage can be harmful — stratified MLE is preferred. **EC-HTE is most valuable precisely when it is most needed — the diagnostic criterion (Claim 3) identifies these scenarios.** **CONFIRMED** by exp-003 full 100 MC (1200 runs, 0 errors). HB crossover at ~11 experts/subgroup; ≥25 recommended for robust performance. Demonstrated with both difference-in-means and CausalForestDML (exp-011: consistent bias reduction pattern, ec_hte_forest |bias|=0.06 vs naive 0.16). CausalForest amplifies the debiasing-hurts effect (up to 5.9x in K=4/extreme) due to nonlinear CATE estimation.\n13\t\n14\t3. **Diagnostic Criterion**: The product of misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity across subgroups provides a computable diagnostic that simultaneously predicts when global correction is harmful (Claim 1) and when the expert label investment for stratified correction is worthwhile (connecting to the budget guidelines from Claim 2). This criterion has standalone value independent of EC-HTE — even without adopting EC-HTE, knowing when global correction backfires is practically actionable.\n15\t\n16\t## Story Spine\n17\t\n18\t- **Problem**: NLP researchers increasingly use LLM annotations as effect modifiers in heterogeneous treatment effect analysis across computational social science (CSS) — e.g., sentiment framing moderates message effectiveness, hate speech type moderates intervention impact. LLM misclassification is non-random — error rates vary by subgroup (Ashwin et al., 2025: error varies by refugee status, gender, education; documented across CSS tasks including sentiment, stance, toxicity). Current PPI/DSL corrections apply global rectifiers assuming homogeneous error.\n19\t\n20\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Mozer (2026) proves arm-specific rectifiers fix ATE bias under differential prediction error, but explicitly limits analysis to average treatment effects. PPI (Angelopoulos et al., 2023) and DSL (Egami et al., 2024) correct population-level estimates. PPCI (Sui et al., 2026) extends PPI to conditional functionals but corrects outcome-side measurement, not covariate-side. ForestIV (Bu et al., 2023) handles ML-covariate measurement error in regression, not CATE. **No work addresses correction when the mismeasured variable defines the heterogeneity structure.**\n21\t\n22\t- **Our framing**: We identify and formalize a previously unrecognized bias mechanism — measurement-error × causal-heterogeneity confounding. When a pooled confusion matrix is applied to correct subgroup-level CATEs, it misattributes prediction noise across subgroups with different error rates, producing bias proportional to the product of misclassification heterogeneity and CATE heterogeneity. This is a problem-level discovery, not a technique-level extension. EC-HTE solves it via hierarchical Bayesian stratified correction with honest causal forest integration. **Novelty positioning**: The individual components (HB Dirichlet estimation, confusion matrix correction, causal forests) are established; the contribution is (a) identifying and formalizing the bias mechanism specific to effect-modifier misclassification, (b) the Δπ×Δτ product characterization that predicts when correction backfires, and (c) bridging the measurement error and HTE literatures in a practically consequential way. Frame as \"problem identification + principled solution\" not \"new estimation technique.\"\n23\t\n24\t- **Headline result template**: \"On semi-synthetic CSS benchmarks, global correction worsens subgroup CATE bias by 2-3x (median), with amplification up to 5.9x for K=4 subgroups; EC-HTE reduces bias to near-zero while maintaining 92-97% coverage, with as few as 250 expert labels. Combined with PPCI, the composition achieves near-zero bias (0.005) even when both covariate and outcome errors are present.\"\n25\t\n26\t- **Oracle framing**: When reporting DGP C results where ec_hte_ppci outperforms oracle, always use \"covariate-oracle\" (true Z + observed Y), never unqualified \"oracle\". Frame as \"composite correction is necessary and sufficient when both error types coexist\" — NOT \"beats oracle\". The result is by construction (ec_hte_ppci corrects both error types; covariate-oracle only corrects one), not surprising.\n27\t\n28\t## Key Contributions (ordered for paper)\n29\t\n30\t1. **Bias decomposition identity**: Exact population-level identity: bias ∝ misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity (Δπ×Δτ product form). NOT a bound — it is an exact identity under A1–A4; finite-sample R² measures MC noise, not bound looseness. Includes \"debiasing can hurt\" proposition with constructive example. Frame as \"bias decomposition\" or \"bias identity\" throughout — never \"bias bound.\" (Theory + Empirical)\n31\t2. **EC-HTE framework**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified misclassification correction + variance-adjusted honest causal forest. (Method)\n32\t3. **Diagnostic criterion**: Computable threshold from pilot data to decide whether stratified correction is needed. (Practical tool)\n33\t4. **EC-HTE + PPCI composition — empirically necessary and sufficient**: EC-HTE and PPCI are empirically necessary and sufficient in composition: neither alone adequately handles dual-error scenarios (DGP C), but their composition reduces bias to near-zero (0.005, a 35× improvement over EC-HTE alone). EC-HTE exploits mixing matrix structure for covariate-side error; PPCI rectifier captures outcome-side error. PPCI alone can partially correct covariate error but with higher variance (limited by gold subset size). In Methods, retain full discussion of partial overlap; in Abstract, lead with \"necessary and sufficient in composition.\" (Method + Empirical)\n34\t5. **Comprehensive validation**: Synthetic + semi-synthetic + real-data case study (pattern consistency, not ground-truth benchmark) with multiple LLMs. (Empirical)\n35\t\n36\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n37\t\n38\t1. **\"Why not just use expert labels directly for CATE?\"** — Defense: 2000 expert labels / k subgroups / honest forest halving → insufficient power per cell. EC-HTE uses all LLM data for low-variance CATE, expert labels only for calibration. Explicitly quantify in experiments.\n39\t\n40\t2. **\"How is this different from PPCI / DSL?\"** — PPCI rectifier is a general-purpose correction that captures any systematic error (covariate + outcome); EC-HTE is a structured correction exploiting mixing matrix structure specifically for covariate-side error. They are complementary: EC-HTE alone is more efficient for covariate error (uses M⁻¹ structure), PPCI alone can partially correct covariate error but with higher variance (limited by gold subset). In composition, EC-HTE handles structured covariate error, residual rectifier handles outcome error. DSL applied per-subgroup is a valid baseline but lacks cross-subgroup shrinkage, operates at estimand level rather than measurement model level, and has strictly higher variance under partial pooling. Do NOT say \"DSL cannot do subgroup correction\" — say it lacks the principled shrinkage mechanism.\n41\t\n42\t3. **\"Incremental over Mozer (2026)\"** — Mozer addresses ATE under differential prediction error. We address CATE under heterogeneous effect-modifier misclassification — a structurally different problem. The bias mechanism we identify (pooled correction hurting low-error subgroups) has no counterpart in Mozer's framework.\n43\t\n44\t4. **\"How sensitive to subgroup definition?\"** — Hierarchical Bayesian partial pooling makes the method robust: with well-defined subgroups, full stratification; with noisy subgroups, automatic shrinkage toward global. Include robustness analysis.\n45\t\n46\t5. **\"Real-world expert label cost\"** — exp-006 provides precise RMSE crossover points: K=2/extreme n_expert=250, K=4/extreme n=1000, K=4/moderate n=2000, K=2/moderate never crosses (global always better on RMSE). Paper needs \"Expert Budget Recommendation\" subsection with per-K guidelines. Key message: when diagnostic criterion flags high heterogeneity (extreme regime), EC-HTE is worth the investment at moderate budgets; when heterogeneity is low, global correction is the safer choice. This honest framing connects Claim 2 (EC-HTE method) to Claim 3 (diagnostic criterion) — the diagnostic decides the correction strategy.\n47\t\n48\t6. **\"How does this differ from Carroll et al. (2006) / classical measurement error?\"** — The qualitative insight that misspecified corrections can amplify MSE is classical (Fuller 1987, Sec. 2.3). Our specific contributions beyond this are: (a) the quantitative Δπ×Δτ product form for CATE estimation with effect-modifier misclassification, (b) demonstrating this failure mode occurs *by default* in standard LLM annotation workflows, and (c) providing a computable diagnostic and correction framework. Must explicitly cite and contextualize: Fuller (1987), Carroll et al. (2006 Ch. 4), Gustafson (2003), Hu & Schennach (2008), Imai & Yamamoto (2010). Also cite Bayesian annotation models: Dawid & Skene, Passonneau & Carpenter (2014), Hovy et al. (2013). **Bibliography target: 30-35 references** spanning measurement error, Bayesian estimation, causal inference, LLM-as-annotator (Tornberg 2024, Gilardi et al. 2023, Ziems et al. 2024), HTE methods (Wager & Athey 2018, Kennedy 2023, Chernozhukov et al. 2018).\n49\t\n50\t7. **\"Methodological novelty is modest\"** — Acknowledge explicitly. Position contribution as problem discovery + formal characterization + comprehensive validation, not as a new estimation technique. HB partial pooling provides meaningful RMSE reduction for moderate subgroups but is NOT \"never worse than global\" — it is a James-Stein shrinkage estimator with known boundary conditions. **Recommended condition**: n_expert per subgroup ≥ ~25 (e.g., n_expert ≥ 100 for K=4 with 12% minority). Below this, stratified MLE is preferred. This honest limitation strengthens credibility. State conditions explicitly using per-subgroup formulation, not just total n_expert.\n51\t\n52\t8. **\"Why no figures?\"** — Paper MUST include key figures: (1) schematic of bias mechanism (global over/under-correction), (2) bias amplification heatmap (Δπ vs Δτ), (3) diagnostic ROC curve, (4) budget crossover curves. Move P2 experiments (exp-008, exp-009) to appendix to free space.\n53\t\n54\t## Venue Fit\n55\t\n56\tEMNLP fit is strong: core NLP application (LLM annotation quality), computational social science use cases (sentiment analysis, hate speech detection, refugee interview coding), direct comparison with NeurIPS/EMNLP published methods (DSL, PPI, benchmarking). Methodology is causal inference but framed through NLP lens. Potential reviewer pool: CL+CSS track. **NOTE**: Framing broadened from \"political-science\" to \"CSS\" (D004b) — TweetEval stance tasks too small (N<1000), sentiment (N=45K) usable but not political science. CSS is more accurate and equally strong for EMNLP.\n57\t\n58\tRisk: pure statistics reviewers may want stronger theoretical contribution (convergence rates, minimax bounds). Mitigation: emphasize the practical diagnostic criterion and empirical validation breadth.\n59\t\n60\t## Writing Requirements (Dream Round 2 consensus)\n61\t\n62\t1. **\"Bias decomposition\" NOT \"bias bound\"** — Theorem 1 is an exact identity at population level. R² < 1.0 in verification reflects finite-sample MC noise, not bound looseness.\n63\t2. **Bibliography: 30-35 references minimum** — Must span 5 literatures: classical measurement error, Bayesian estimation, causal inference, LLM-as-annotator, CSS. Critical citations: Fuller 1987, Wager & Athey 2018, Imai & Yamamoto 2010.\n64\t3. **3+ figures in main text** — (a) bias mechanism schematic, (b) Δπ×Δτ amplification heatmap, (c) diagnostic ROC curve, (d) budget crossover curves. Move exp-008/exp-009 tables to appendix.\n65\t4. **Semi-synthetic DGP fully specified** — outcome generation, treatment assignment, CATE injection mechanism.\n66\t5. **Real-data framed as pattern consistency** — NOT ground-truth benchmark. No bias/RMSE against unknown true CATEs.\n67\t6. **EC-HTE advantage is conditional, not universal** — ec_hte dominates when misclassification heterogeneity is high (extreme regime) OR n_expert is large (≥500). In moderate regime with small n_expert (~100), global correction can outperform ec_hte because per-subgroup CM estimation noise exceeds the benefit of stratification. This connects to Claim 3: the diagnostic criterion (Δπ×Δτ) predicts when EC-HTE is needed. Unified condition: n_expert/K ≥ ~25-50 experts per subgroup.\n68\t11. **RMSE tradeoff must be disclosed** — ec_hte has higher RMSE than global/naive in K=4/n≤100 configs (up to 3.5x in extreme cases) due to noisy per-subgroup CM estimation. Bias is lower but variance is higher. Must report both bias AND RMSE; include bias-RMSE tradeoff analysis. At n_expert≥500, ec_hte RMSE becomes competitive.\n69\t12. **K-dependence of debiasing-hurts** — DIM estimator: K=2 extreme ~2.86×, K=4 extreme ~2.41× (does NOT monotonically increase with K). CausalForest: K=4 extreme up to 5.9× (nonlinear estimator amplifies with more subgroups). Report both patterns; do NOT claim \"more subgroups → always worse\" without qualifying the estimator.\n70\t7. **Confusion matrix invertibility** — State det(Ĉ_k) ≠ 0 assumption explicitly.\n71\t8. **Diagnostic AUC cross-validated** — Leave-one-setting-out or held-out evaluation, not in-sample.\n72\t9. **Hyperprior values stated + sensitivity analysis** — Gamma(α, β) for Dirichlet concentration; report sensitivity to 2× changes.\n73\t10. **PPCI complementarity elevated** — Highlight in abstract and contributions. Frame as \"complementary\" not \"orthogonal\": EC-HTE is structured covariate-error correction; PPCI rectifier is general residual correction. Composition = EC-HTE handles structured part + rectifier handles remainder (primarily outcome error).\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4aab4440-3f1a-4989-8d2a-6845e346e8e8","uuid":"8eff1721-6259-43ac-abc2-38c47503e5f0","timestamp":"2026-05-23T19:39:38.468Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122454/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — ec_hte_llm_annotation\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Deadline: ARR submission May 25, 2026; commitment deadline August 2, 2026\n- Format: Long paper, 8 pages + unlimited references\n\n## Core Claims (3 条，可证伪)\n\n1. **Bias Mechanism Discovery**: When LLM misclassification rates for an effect modifier vary across subgroups, applying a global (pooled) correction to subgroup-level CATE estimates introduces systematic bias — over-correcting low-error subgroups and under-correcting high-error ones. In realistic settings, this \"debiasing\" can worsen CATE bias by 2-3x (median across configurations), with amplification up to 5.9x for K=4 subgroups; when naive bias is near zero, global correction creates bias where none existed. For the difference-in-means estimator, the amplification magnitude does NOT monotonically increase with K (K=2 extreme: up to 2.86× vs K=4 extreme: up to 2.41×); however, with nonlinear estimators such as CausalForest, more subgroups amplify the effect substantially (K=4/extreme: up to 5.9×) due to compounding estimation noise in tree-based CATE. Global correction increases subgroup-level bias in ~50% of the parameter space.\n\n2. **EC-HTE Solution**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified correction (EC-HTE) substantially reduces subgroup-level bias when misclassification heterogeneity is sufficiently high, while controlling estimation variance through partial pooling. HB provides meaningful RMSE reduction by borrowing strength across groups (classic James-Stein shrinkage). We provide precise crossover thresholds: EC-HTE outperforms global correction in RMSE with as few as 250 expert labels (K=2, high heterogeneity), scaling to ~1000 for K=4. **Boundary condition**: when expert labels per subgroup < ~25, shrinkage can be harmful — stratified MLE is preferred. **EC-HTE is most valuable precisely when it is most needed — the diagnostic criterion (Claim 3) identifies these scenarios.** **CONFIRMED** by exp-003 full 100 MC (1200 runs, 0 errors). HB crossover at ~11 experts/subgroup; ≥25 recommended for robust performance. Demonstrated with both difference-in-means and CausalForestDML (exp-011: consistent bias reduction pattern, ec_hte_forest |bias|=0.06 vs naive 0.16). CausalForest amplifies the debiasing-hurts effect (up to 5.9x in K=4/extreme) due to nonlinear CATE estimation.\n\n3. **Diagnostic Criterion**: The product of misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity across subgroups provides a computable diagnostic that simultaneously predicts when global correction is harmful (Claim 1) and when the expert label investment for stratified correction is worthwhile (connecting to the budget guidelines from Claim 2). This criterion has standalone value independent of EC-HTE — even without adopting EC-HTE, knowing when global correction backfires is practically actionable.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: NLP researchers increasingly use LLM annotations as effect modifiers in heterogeneous treatment effect analysis across computational social science (CSS) — e.g., sentiment framing moderates message effectiveness, hate speech type moderates intervention impact. LLM misclassification is non-random — error rates vary by subgroup (Ashwin et al., 2025: error varies by refugee status, gender, education; documented across CSS tasks including sentiment, stance, toxicity). Current PPI/DSL corrections apply global rectifiers assuming homogeneous error.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Mozer (2026) proves arm-specific rectifiers fix ATE bias under differential prediction error, but explicitly limits analysis to average treatment effects. PPI (Angelopoulos et al., 2023) and DSL (Egami et al., 2024) correct population-level estimates. PPCI (Sui et al., 2026) extends PPI to conditional functionals but corrects outcome-side measurement, not covariate-side. ForestIV (Bu et al., 2023) handles ML-covariate measurement error in regression, not CATE. **No work addresses correction when the mismeasured variable defines the heterogeneity structure.**\n\n- **Our framing**: We identify and formalize a previously unrecognized bias mechanism — measurement-error × causal-heterogeneity confounding. When a pooled confusion matrix is applied to correct subgroup-level CATEs, it misattributes prediction noise across subgroups with different error rates, producing bias proportional to the product of misclassification heterogeneity and CATE heterogeneity. This is a problem-level discovery, not a technique-level extension. EC-HTE solves it via hierarchical Bayesian stratified correction with honest causal forest integration. **Novelty positioning**: The individual components (HB Dirichlet estimation, confusion matrix correction, causal forests) are established; the contribution is (a) identifying and formalizing the bias mechanism specific to effect-modifier misclassification, (b) the Δπ×Δτ product characterization that predicts when correction backfires, and (c) bridging the measurement error and HTE literatures in a practically consequential way. Frame as \"problem identification + principled solution\" not \"new estimation technique.\"\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"On semi-synthetic CSS benchmarks, global correction worsens subgroup CATE bias by 2-3x (median), with amplification up to 5.9x for K=4 subgroups; EC-HTE reduces bias to near-zero while maintaining 92-97% coverage, with as few as 250 expert labels. Combined with PPCI, the composition achieves near-zero bias (0.005) even when both covariate and outcome errors are present.\"\n\n- **Oracle framing**: When reporting DGP C results where ec_hte_ppci outperforms oracle, always use \"covariate-oracle\" (true Z + observed Y), never unqualified \"oracle\". Frame as \"composite correction is necessary and sufficient when both error types coexist\" — NOT \"beats oracle\". The result is by construction (ec_hte_ppci corrects both error types; covariate-oracle only corrects one), not surprising.\n\n## Key Contributions (ordered for paper)\n\n1. **Bias decomposition identity**: Exact population-level identity: bias ∝ misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity (Δπ×Δτ product form). NOT a bound — it is an exact identity under A1–A4; finite-sample R² measures MC noise, not bound looseness. Includes \"debiasing can hurt\" proposition with constructive example. Frame as \"bias decomposition\" or \"bias identity\" throughout — never \"bias bound.\" (Theory + Empirical)\n2. **EC-HTE framework**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified misclassification correction + variance-adjusted honest causal forest. (Method)\n3. **Diagnostic criterion**: Computable threshold from pilot data to decide whether stratified correction is needed. (Practical tool)\n4. **EC-HTE + PPCI composition — empirically necessary and sufficient**: EC-HTE and PPCI are empirically necessary and sufficient in composition: neither alone adequately handles dual-error scenarios (DGP C), but their composition reduces bias to near-zero (0.005, a 35× improvement over EC-HTE alone). EC-HTE exploits mixing matrix structure for covariate-side error; PPCI rectifier captures outcome-side error. PPCI alone can partially correct covariate error but with higher variance (limited by gold subset size). In Methods, retain full discussion of partial overlap; in Abstract, lead with \"necessary and sufficient in composition.\" (Method + Empirical)\n5. **Comprehensive validation**: Synthetic + semi-synthetic + real-data case study (pattern consistency, not ground-truth benchmark) with multiple LLMs. (Empirical)\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. **\"Why not just use expert labels directly for CATE?\"** — Defense: 2000 expert labels / k subgroups / honest forest halving → insufficient power per cell. EC-HTE uses all LLM data for low-variance CATE, expert labels only for calibration. Explicitly quantify in experiments.\n\n2. **\"How is this different from PPCI / DSL?\"** — PPCI rectifier is a general-purpose correction that captures any systematic error (covariate + outcome); EC-HTE is a structured correction exploiting mixing matrix structure specifically for covariate-side error. They are complementary: EC-HTE alone is more efficient for covariate error (uses M⁻¹ structure), PPCI alone can partially correct covariate error but with higher variance (limited by gold subset). In composition, EC-HTE handles structured covariate error, residual rectifier handles outcome error. DSL applied per-subgroup is a valid baseline but lacks cross-subgroup shrinkage, operates at estimand level rather than measurement model level, and has strictly higher variance under partial pooling. Do NOT say \"DSL cannot do subgroup correction\" — say it lacks the principled shrinkage mechanism.\n\n3. **\"Incremental over Mozer (2026)\"** — Mozer addresses ATE under differential prediction error. We address CATE under heterogeneous effect-modifier misclassification — a structurally different problem. The bias mechanism we identify (pooled correction hurting low-error subgroups) has no counterpart in Mozer's framework.\n\n4. **\"How sensitive to subgroup definition?\"** — Hierarchical Bayesian partial pooling makes the method robust: with well-defined subgroups, full stratification; with noisy subgroups, automatic shrinkage toward global. Include robustness analysis.\n\n5. **\"Real-world expert label cost\"** — exp-006 provides precise RMSE crossover points: K=2/extreme n_expert=250, K=4/extreme n=1000, K=4/moderate n=2000, K=2/moderate never crosses (global always better on RMSE). Paper needs \"Expert Budget Recommendation\" subsection with per-K guidelines. Key message: when diagnostic criterion flags high heterogeneity (extreme regime), EC-HTE is worth the investment at moderate budgets; when heterogeneity is low, global correction is the safer choice. This honest framing connects Claim 2 (EC-HTE method) to Claim 3 (diagnostic criterion) — the diagnostic decides the correction strategy.\n\n6. **\"How does this differ from Carroll et al. (2006) / classical measurement error?\"** — The qualitative insight that misspecified corrections can amplify MSE is classical (Fuller 1987, Sec. 2.3). Our specific contributions beyond this are: (a) the quantitative Δπ×Δτ product form for CATE estimation with effect-modifier misclassification, (b) demonstrating this failure mode occurs *by default* in standard LLM annotation workflows, and (c) providing a computable diagnostic and correction framework. Must explicitly cite and contextualize: Fuller (1987), Carroll et al. (2006 Ch. 4), Gustafson (2003), Hu & Schennach (2008), Imai & Yamamoto (2010). Also cite Bayesian annotation models: Dawid & Skene, Passonneau & Carpenter (2014), Hovy et al. (2013). **Bibliography target: 30-35 references** spanning measurement error, Bayesian estimation, causal inference, LLM-as-annotator (Tornberg 2024, Gilardi et al. 2023, Ziems et al. 2024), HTE methods (Wager & Athey 2018, Kennedy 2023, Chernozhukov et al. 2018).\n\n7. **\"Methodological novelty is modest\"** — Acknowledge explicitly. Position contribution as problem discovery + formal characterization + comprehensive validation, not as a new estimation technique. HB partial pooling provides meaningful RMSE reduction for moderate subgroups but is NOT \"never worse than global\" — it is a James-Stein shrinkage estimator with known boundary conditions. **Recommended condition**: n_expert per subgroup ≥ ~25 (e.g., n_expert ≥ 100 for K=4 with 12% minority). Below this, stratified MLE is preferred. This honest limitation strengthens credibility. State conditions explicitly using per-subgroup formulation, not just total n_expert.\n\n8. **\"Why no figures?\"** — Paper MUST include key figures: (1) schematic of bias mechanism (global over/under-correction), (2) bias amplification heatmap (Δπ vs Δτ), (3) diagnostic ROC curve, (4) budget crossover curves. Move P2 experiments (exp-008, exp-009) to appendix to free space.\n\n## Venue Fit\n\nEMNLP fit is strong: core NLP application (LLM annotation quality), computational social science use cases (sentiment analysis, hate speech detection, refugee interview coding), direct comparison with NeurIPS/EMNLP published methods (DSL, PPI, benchmarking). Methodology is causal inference but framed through NLP lens. Potential reviewer pool: CL+CSS track. **NOTE**: Framing broadened from \"political-science\" to \"CSS\" (D004b) — TweetEval stance tasks too small (N<1000), sentiment (N=45K) usable but not political science. CSS is more accurate and equally strong for EMNLP.\n\nRisk: pure statistics reviewers may want stronger theoretical contribution (convergence rates, minimax bounds). Mitigation: emphasize the practical diagnostic criterion and empirical validation breadth.\n\n## Writing Requirements (Dream Round 2 consensus)\n\n1. **\"Bias decomposition\" NOT \"bias bound\"** — Theorem 1 is an exact identity at population level. R² < 1.0 in verification reflects finite-sample MC noise, not bound looseness.\n2. **Bibliography: 30-35 references minimum** — Must span 5 literatures: classical measurement error, Bayesian estimation, causal inference, LLM-as-annotator, CSS. Critical citations: Fuller 1987, Wager & Athey 2018, Imai & Yamamoto 2010.\n3. **3+ figures in main text** — (a) bias mechanism schematic, (b) Δπ×Δτ amplification heatmap, (c) diagnostic ROC curve, (d) budget crossover curves. Move exp-008/exp-009 tables to appendix.\n4. **Semi-synthetic DGP fully specified** — outcome generation, treatment assignment, CATE injection mechanism.\n5. **Real-data framed as pattern consistency** — NOT ground-truth benchmark. No bias/RMSE against unknown true CATEs.\n6. **EC-HTE advantage is conditional, not universal** — ec_hte dominates when misclassification heterogeneity is high (extreme regime) OR n_expert is large (≥500). In moderate regime with small n_expert (~100), global correction can outperform ec_hte because per-subgroup CM estimation noise exceeds the benefit of stratification. This connects to Claim 3: the diagnostic criterion (Δπ×Δτ) predicts when EC-HTE is needed. Unified condition: n_expert/K ≥ ~25-50 experts per subgroup.\n11. **RMSE tradeoff must be disclosed** — ec_hte has higher RMSE than global/naive in K=4/n≤100 configs (up to 3.5x in extreme cases) due to noisy per-subgroup CM estimation. Bias is lower but variance is higher. Must report both bias AND RMSE; include bias-RMSE tradeoff analysis. At n_expert≥500, ec_hte RMSE becomes competitive.\n12. **K-dependence of debiasing-hurts** — DIM estimator: K=2 extreme ~2.86×, K=4 extreme ~2.41× (does NOT monotonically increase with K). CausalForest: K=4 extreme up to 5.9× (nonlinear estimator amplifies with more subgroups). Report both patterns; do NOT claim \"more subgroups → always worse\" without qualifying the estimator.\n7. **Confusion matrix invertibility** — State det(Ĉ_k) ≠ 0 assumption explicitly.\n8. **Diagnostic AUC cross-validated** — Leave-one-setting-out or held-out evaluation, not in-sample.\n9. **Hyperprior values stated + sensitivity analysis** — Gamma(α, β) for Dirichlet concentration; report sensitivity to 2× changes.\n10. **PPCI complementarity elevated** — Highlight in abstract and contributions. Frame as \"complementary\" not \"orthogonal\": EC-HTE is structured covariate-error correction; PPCI rectifier is general residual correction. Composition = EC-HTE handles structured part + rectifier handles remainder (primarily outcome error).\n","numLines":74,"startLine":1,"totalLines":74}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019wUCX4kn9BRY6HmSrb77fS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a very thorough understanding of the project, the median tier definition, and all the experiments (both planned and completed). Let me construct the detailed predicted results for each experiment in the experiment_plan under the median tier scenario.\n\nThe key median tier characteristics:\n- excitement: 3.0-3.5\n- soundness: 3.5-4.0\n- overall: 3.0-3.5\n- claim1 (bias identity) accepted: 75-90%\n- claim2 (EC-HTE useful) accepted: 40-60%\n- claim3 (diagnostic) accepted: 30-50%\n\n\n- perceived novelty: 2.5-3.5\n- major weaknesses per review: 1-2\n\nReviewers will likely view the bias identity work as a straightforward application of existing methods, see the EC-HTE approach as having a narrow operating regime, find the diagnostic setting-level analysis unconvincing, and note that real-data EC-HTE doesn't outperform the global baseline with a significant RMSE tradeoff. The negative results on real causal models will be accepted as honest findings rather than fatal flaws.\n\nGenerating the full YAML output...\n\nI'm grounding each experiment's predicted results in the actual registry data, then explaining through the median-tier framing why these outcomes collectively point to a solid but not exceptional contribution. For the hierarchical Bayes EC-HTE work, the results are strong but reviewers will see it as a standard James-Stein estimator application. The bias identity experiments show high R² but get framed as a formalization of Fuller-Carroll. Semi-synthetic results work but have boundary condition issues. Real data is where EC-HTE breaks down—a major weakness. The diagnostic setting-level analysis hits AUC=0.49, another significant problem. Budget sensitivity reveals how restrictive the operating conditions are. The PPCI+DSL composition works but feels secondary to the core claims. Multi-LLM experiments support the general premise without strengthening the main arguments. Adaptive allocation is cut off but likely follows the pattern of limited gains.\n\nNow I'm moving through the remaining experiments—robustness testing shows graceful degradation with coverage as the key metric, and the CausalForest comparison demonstrates 5.9x amplification at the cost of RMSE penalties. With these pieces in place, I'm ready to write out the full YAML structure.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14733,"cache_read_input_tokens":44077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14733},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4aab4440-3f1a-4989-8d2a-6845e346e8e8","uuid":"fbd188b3-6844-4803-babd-54f3f8f4d311"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019wUCX4kn9BRY6HmSrb77fS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Problem framing 有吸引力但 novelty perception 分裂：部分 reviewer 认为 'correction can hurt' \n  是 known intuition 的 formalization，EC-HTE 的 narrow operating regime 削弱 practical impact，\n  diagnostic 在 setting level 不 work。需要调整 claims 强度——Claim 1 降级为 'first formal \n  characterization of classical ME amplification in LLM annotation pipelines'，Claim 2 降级为 \n  'proof-of-concept correction demonstrating the identity is actionable'，Claim 3 承认 diagnostic \n  仅在 subgroup level 有效。补充实验方向：找一个 EC-HTE 在 real data 上 works 的案例。\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE on synthetic data: HB Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator \n      with partial pooling, compare against MLE/Laplace on full regime sweep (extreme/moderate/homogeneous \n      × n_expert 100-2000 × K=2,4 subgroups). 3600 MC runs.\n    expected_results:\n      mcmc_rhat_max: 1.024\n      mcmc_ess_min: 129\n      mcmc_divergent: 0\n      runtime_min: 69\n      total_mc_runs: 3600\n      hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50: \"4-9%\"\n      hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100: \"1-2%\"\n      hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate: \"6-9%\"\n      hb_coverage_min: 0.87\n      hb_coverage_median: 0.93\n      k4_extreme_n50_hb_rmse: 0.99\n      hyperprior_sensitivity_k2_rmse_variation: \"<1%\"\n      hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_rmse_variation: \"~4-5%\"\n      hyperprior_sensitivity_coverage_invariant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      HB partial pooling 在 synthetic DGP 上 works as expected——这是 James-Stein shrinkage 的\n      standard result，reviewer 不会对此感到 surprised。K=2 improvement 4-9% modest，K=4/extreme/n=50 \n      曾出现 singularity blowup（修复后 RMSE 从 509→0.27），但 reviewer 会将此视为 implementation \n      issue 而非 fundamental limitation。Coverage 0.87-0.93 reasonable 但未达 nominal 0.95。\n      Median reviewer 评价：technically sound (Soundness 3.5-4.0) 但 novelty 不高——HB Dirichlet \n      partial pooling 是 established technique (Gelman et al. BDA3)，improvement 幅度 modest，\n      且 hyperprior sensitivity at K=4 (~4-5%) 暗示 method 对 specification 有一定 sensitivity。\n      这个实验支持 Claim 2 的 technical validity 但不足以让 reviewer 认为 method 有 substantial \n      practical value。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=2)\"\n        columns: [\"n_expert\", \"Regime\", \"Subgroup\", \"MLE RMSE\", \"HB RMSE\", \"Δ%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"50\", \"extreme\", \"z0\", \"0.142\", \"0.131\", \"-7.7%\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"extreme\", \"z1\", \"0.156\", \"0.142\", \"-9.0%\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"moderate\", \"z0\", \"0.098\", \"0.094\", \"-4.1%\"]\n          - [\"100\", \"extreme\", \"z0\", \"0.095\", \"0.093\", \"-2.1%\"]\n          - [\"100\", \"extreme\", \"z1\", \"0.108\", \"0.107\", \"-0.9%\"]\n          - [\"250\", \"extreme\", \"z0\", \"0.068\", \"0.067\", \"-1.5%\"]\n          - [\"500\", \"extreme\", \"z0\", \"0.048\", \"0.048\", \"-0.0%\"]\n      - name: \"Table 4: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=4)\"\n        columns: [\"n_expert\", \"Regime\", \"Worst Subgroup\", \"MLE RMSE\", \"HB RMSE\", \"Δ%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"50\", \"extreme\", \"D(π=0.30)\", \"1.32\", \"0.99\", \"-25.0%\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"moderate\", \"C\", \"0.186\", \"0.170\", \"-8.6%\"]\n          - [\"100\", \"extreme\", \"D(π=0.30)\", \"0.38\", \"0.29\", \"-23.7%\"]\n          - [\"250\", \"extreme\", \"D\", \"0.135\", \"0.128\", \"-5.2%\"]\n          - [\"500\", \"all\", \"all\", \"~0.07\", \"~0.07\", \"<0.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"No figures from this experiment in main text; data feeds into budget crossover curves (Figure 4)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reviewer 对 exp-001 的反应分两极：measurement error / causal inference 背景的 reviewer \n      认为 HB Dirichlet-Multinomial partial pooling 是 textbook technique（BDA3 Ch. 5），\n      improvement 仅 4-9%（K=2）到 25%（K=4/extreme worst-case），不构成 methodological \n      contribution。NLP 背景 reviewer 可能认为 3600 MC runs 的 thoroughness 是 strength。\n      Coverage 0.87-0.93 是 concern——未达 nominal 95%，reviewer 会问 why。Hyperprior \n      sensitivity at K=4 (~4-5%) 被视为 acceptable 但需要 disclosure。Overall：支持 soundness \n      score 3.5-4.0，但不显著提升 excitement。\n\n  - name: \"Formal Bias Identity Verification\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      Derive bias = f(Δπ, Δτ) analytically, verify empirically across systematic parameter grid. \n      Produce 'debiasing can hurt' proposition with constructive two-subgroup example. K>2 extension.\n    expected_results:\n      r2_k2: 0.9939\n      r2_k4: 0.9738\n      tightness_ratio_k2_median: 1.0027\n      tightness_ratio_k4_median: 1.0234\n      debiasing_hurts_pct: 50\n      debiasing_hurts_threshold_delta_misclass: 0.1235\n      max_bias_ratio_k2: 2.86\n      max_bias_ratio_k4: 2.41\n      coverage_2se_k2: 0.951\n      coverage_2se_k4: 0.940\n      total_configs: 520\n    result_rationale: >\n      R²>0.97 confirms the identity is exact at population level——finite-sample MC noise 解释 \n      remaining variance。这是 paper 最强的 technical result：product form Bias ∝ Δπ×Δτ 是 exact \n      identity, not a bound。但 median reviewer 会有 novelty concern——至少一位 reviewer 有 \n      measurement error / causal inference 背景，认为这是 Fuller (1987) / Carroll (2006) 在 LLM \n      场景的 straightforward application。Qualitative insight \"correction can hurt when error is \n      heterogeneous\" 是 known (Fuller 1987, Sec 2.3: \"misspecified corrections amplify MSE\")。\n      Paper 的 contribution 是 (a) quantitative product form 和 (b) application to LLM annotation \n      pipelines。Debiasing hurts in 50% of parameter space 是 striking 但需要 qualification——\n      这 50% 包括所有 delta_misclass > 0.1235 的 configs，reviewer 问 \"how often does this \n      occur in practice?\"。Max amplification 2.86× (K=2) 和 2.41× (K=4) 的 non-monotonic \n      K-dependence 是 nuanced result，但 reviewer 可能 view this as \"moderate\" amplification \n      rather than \"dramatic\"。总体：claim1 被 75-90% reviewer 接受为 valid contribution，但 \n      perceived novelty 被 downweight 到 2.5-3.5 因为 formal novelty modest。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Bias Identity Verification (R²)\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"R²\", \"Tightness Ratio (median)\", \"Tightness Ratio (max)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"2\", \"0.994\", \"1.003\", \"1.021\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"0.974\", \"1.023\", \"1.089\"]\n      - name: \"Table 2: Debiasing Hurts Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"K=2\", \"K=4\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Configs where global hurts (%)\", \"50%\", \"50%\"]\n          - [\"Max bias amplification (DIM)\", \"2.86×\", \"2.41×\"]\n          - [\"Δπ threshold for hurt\", \"0.124\", \"0.124\"]\n          - [\"Coverage (2SE)\", \"0.951\", \"0.940\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: Δπ × Δτ bias amplification heatmap — color intensity shows bias ratio (global/naive), red region = debiasing hurts. Clear product-form structure visible.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 paper 的 theoretical backbone。Median reviewer 给 Soundness 3.5-4.0 因为 verification \n      thorough（520 configs, R²>0.97）。但 Excitement 因 novelty concern 被压到 3.0-3.5。\n      关键分歧点：NLP reviewer 可能认为 \"previously unrecognized bias mechanism\" 是 fair claim；\n      statistics reviewer 认为 qualitative insight is classical，quantitative form 只是 \n      routine derivation in a new application context。Paper 需要 explicitly acknowledge \n      Fuller/Carroll precedent 来 preempt 这个 objection（median framing 已 suggest \n      降级 claim wording）。50% hurt rate 和 2.86× max amplification 虽然 noteworthy \n      但不足以让 skeptical reviewer 升 excitement score——需要 real-data demonstration \n      that this actually matters。\n\n  - name: \"Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      Semi-synthetic benchmark using real CSS tweet corpus (TweetEval sentiment, N=45K). Inject \n      known CATE heterogeneity structure, annotate with GPT-4.1, apply EC-HTE vs baselines. \n      K=4 subgroups with misclass rates S0=0.05 to S3=0.25.\n    expected_results:\n      n_subgroups: 4\n      misclass_rates: \"S0=0.05, S1=0.10, S2=0.15, S3=0.25\"\n      delta_pi: 0.20\n      debiasing_hurts_confirmed: true\n      mc_runs: 100\n      hb_vs_mle_n50_S3_extreme_rmse_change: \"-57% (HB worse)\"\n      hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme_rmse_change: \"+60% (HB dramatically better)\"\n      hb_vs_mle_n250_S3_rmse_change: \"+5-17% (HB better)\"\n      hb_crossover: \"n_expert=100 per subgroup\"\n      boundary_condition: \"n_expert>=100 recommended; n=50 with extreme heterogeneity in tiny subgroups (12%) shows moderate degradation\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Semi-synthetic 设计 validates the bias identity in a more realistic setting——real text \n      corpus + injected CATE heterogeneity。Key finding: HB crossover at ~n=100 per subgroup \n      (≥25 experts/subgroup for 12% minority subgroups)。Reviewer 接受 semi-synthetic 作为 \n      valid evaluation framework 但注意到几个 concerns：(1) DGP 设计有 degrees of freedom——\n      misclass rates S0=0.05 to S3=0.25 创造了 ideal conditions for EC-HTE (Δπ=0.20 is \"extreme\")。\n      (2) n=50 boundary condition (HB worse by 57% at S3) 是 significant practical limitation——\n      K=4 with 12% minority means only 6 expert labels per subgroup，too few for reliable CM \n      estimation。(3) Semi-synthetic 不能 fully substitute for real-data validation。Reviewer \n      认为这个实验是 necessary but not sufficient for Claim 2。Pattern 与 exp-001 consistent，\n      支持 technical soundness。但 \"sweet spot is n=100-250\" 意味着 realistic expert budgets \n      are 400-1000 for K=4——reviewer 质疑 feasibility。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Semi-Synthetic EC-HTE Performance (K=4, extreme)\"\n        columns: [\"n_expert\", \"Method\", \"Subgroup\", \"|Bias|\", \"RMSE\", \"Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"50\", \"Naive\", \"S3(π=0.25)\", \"0.048\", \"0.109\", \"0.87\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"Global\", \"S3\", \"0.110\", \"0.140\", \"0.92\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"MLE\", \"S3\", \"0.085\", \"0.280\", \"0.90\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"HB\", \"S3\", \"0.072\", \"0.292\", \"0.93\"]\n          - [\"100\", \"HB\", \"S3\", \"0.018\", \"0.112\", \"0.94\"]\n          - [\"100\", \"Global\", \"S3\", \"0.105\", \"0.138\", \"0.92\"]\n          - [\"250\", \"HB\", \"S3\", \"0.009\", \"0.074\", \"0.95\"]\n          - [\"500\", \"HB\", \"all avg\", \"0.005\", \"0.052\", \"0.95\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Data feeds into Figure 4 (budget crossover curves)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Semi-synthetic 是 most controlled validation——reviewer 认为 technically sound 但 asks \n      \"how representative is this DGP?\" Δπ=0.20 是 extreme regime，而 exp-012 pilot 显示 \n      real GPT-4.1 的 Δπ=0.098 only (moderate)。这暗示 paper 的 headline numbers (near-zero \n      bias at n=250) 对应的是 favorable conditions，real-world performance 会 worse。Claim 2 \n      accepted as useful by 40-60%：technical validity 无争议，但 practical utility window \n      被认为 narrow。\n\n  - name: \"Real-Data Case Study (Pattern Consistency)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Apply EC-HTE to UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech corpus (N=2496). Show pattern consistency \n      with synthetic results. Framed as illustrative application, NOT ground-truth benchmark.\n    expected_results:\n      dataset: \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\"\n      n_comments: 2496\n      subgroups: 4\n      delta_pi: 0.117\n      global_FPR: 0.139\n      global_FNR: 0.533\n      avg_abs_bias_naive: 0.210\n      avg_abs_bias_global: 0.273\n      avg_abs_bias_ec_hte: 0.313\n      ec_hte_outperforms_global: false\n      cate_comparison: \"EC-HTE does not outperform global — high FNR (53%) and wide CIs limit correction effectiveness\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 median tier 的 critical weakness。EC-HTE avg |bias| 0.313 > global 0.273 > naive 0.210 \n      ——method 在 real data 上 makes things worse。Root cause：(1) global FNR=0.533 (LLM 严重 \n      under-classifies dehumanization)，近乎 random for positive class，CM inversion amplifies \n      noise；(2) Δπ=0.117 is moderate, not extreme；(3) subgroup-level expert labels insufficient。\n      Paper 将此 frame 为 \"operating condition mismatch\" 和 \"illustrative application\"，但 \n      reviewer 的反应是：这恰好是 the kind of real-world setting where practitioners would \n      apply the method。如果 method 仅在 carefully controlled synthetic conditions 下 work，\n      practical impact 严重受限。至少一位 reviewer 将此视为 major weakness，directly 影响 \n      Claim 2 acceptance rate (40-60%) 和 overall excitement (3.0-3.5)。Honest reporting \n      被 appreciated (S3 in review) 但不 mitigate the fundamental concern。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 12: Real-Data Case Study — UC Berkeley Hate Speech\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Avg |Bias|\", \"Subgroup Max |Bias|\", \"Mean CI Width\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Naive\", \"0.210\", \"0.35\", \"0.18\"]\n          - [\"Global Corrected\", \"0.273\", \"0.42\", \"0.22\"]\n          - [\"EC-HTE (HB)\", \"0.313\", \"0.51\", \"0.34\"]\n      - name: \"Table 13: Subgroup Misclassification Rates\"\n        columns: [\"Subgroup\", \"FPR\", \"FNR\", \"Overall Error\", \"n\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"plat0_long\", \"0.064\", \"0.468\", \"0.266\", \"624\"]\n          - [\"plat0_short\", \"0.101\", \"0.573\", \"0.337\", \"624\"]\n          - [\"plat23_long\", \"0.077\", \"0.530\", \"0.303\", \"624\"]\n          - [\"plat23_short\", \"0.139\", \"0.627\", \"0.383\", \"624\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"No figure; results presented as tables only. Reviewer W5 notes absence of figures as presentation weakness.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-004 是 median tier 最被 reviewer 攻击的实验。W2 (Major) in review: \"EC-HTE's average \n      absolute bias (0.313) is worse than both naive (0.210) and global corrected (0.273).\" \n      Paper 的 defense (\"operating condition mismatch\") 在逻辑上成立（FNR=53% violates \n      practical CM invertibility），但 reviewer 反问：\"how often do real datasets satisfy \n      the conditions?\" 这直接压低 Claim 2 acceptance 到 40-60%。exp-015/016 的 negative \n      results 进一步 confirm：neither low-FNR (gpt-3.5) nor low-FPR (GPT-4.1) real CMs \n      enable EC-HTE to beat global when P(Z=1)=0.18。Median reviewer 接受 honest disclosure \n      但给 excitement 3.0——\"the method fails outside carefully controlled synthetic conditions.\"\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Criterion Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Compute Δπ × Δτ product from pilot data across all settings. ROC analysis of threshold \n      for predicting when global correction fails. Cross-validated evaluation.\n    expected_results:\n      subgroup_level_auc: 0.833\n      subgroup_level_correlation: 0.86\n      setting_level_auc: 0.49\n      low_pi_hurt_pct: 84.6\n      high_pi_hurt_pct: 15.4\n      theory_alignment: \"consistent with exp-002 formula\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Setting-level AUC=0.49 是 median tier 的 second critical weakness。Diagnostic 在 practitioner \n      实际需要做决策的 granularity（\"should I use EC-HTE for this analysis?\"）上 no better than \n      random。Subgroup-level AUC=0.833 表面上 impressive，但 reviewer 指出两个问题：(1) subgroup-level \n      decision 需要已知 subgroup structure，而 knowing which subgroups exist 本身就需要 domain \n      knowledge——循环论证；(2) AUC 0.833 with ~15% false positive rate means 1 in 7 flagged \n      subgroups is false alarm。Claim 3 accepted by only 30-50% of reviewers。Paper 的 reframe \n      (\"two-stage decision workflow: flag subgroups → consult budget\") partially mitigates but \n      doesn't resolve the fundamental gap。Reviewer 建议 explore alternative diagnostic statistics \n      or acknowledge diagnostic is subgroup-level only。This experiment 直接决定了 Claim 3 的 fate \n      in median tier。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Diagnostic Criterion Performance\"\n        columns: [\"Level\", \"AUC\", \"Correlation\", \"Precision@0.5\", \"Recall@0.5\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Subgroup-level\", \"0.833\", \"0.86\", \"0.78\", \"0.85\"]\n          - [\"Setting-level (CV)\", \"0.49\", \"0.12\", \"0.51\", \"0.48\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3: Subgroup-level ROC curve for Δπ×Δτ diagnostic. Shows reasonable discrimination at subgroup level (AUC=0.83) but would need separate panel showing setting-level failure (AUC=0.49) for honest presentation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-005 的 split result 是 median tier 的 defining feature。Strong subgroup AUC + failed \n      setting AUC creates a narrative tension：the diagnostic works where you already know the \n      answer (subgroup level) but fails where you need it most (setting level)。Reviewer W1 (Major): \n      \"Contribution 3 in the introduction leads with 'AUC=0.83' without immediately clarifying \n      this is subgroup-level only — this creates a misleading first impression.\" Paper 需要 \n      reframe Claim 3 更 carefully——lead with setting-level failure, then present subgroup-level \n      as partial recovery。This is the key revision request for median tier.\n\n  - name: \"Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Systematic sweep n_expert ∈ {50, 100, 250, 500, 1000, 2000} × K ∈ {2, 4} × regime. \n      Find crossover point where EC-HTE > Global on RMSE. Validate HB partial pooling value.\n    expected_results:\n      total_rows: 288\n      runtime_min: 110\n      crossover_K2_extreme: 250\n      crossover_K2_moderate: \"never\"\n      crossover_K4_extreme: 1000\n      crossover_K4_moderate: 2000\n      hb_vs_mle_win_rate: \"21/24 (87.5%)\"\n      hb_best_improvement_over_mle: \"+42.4% RMSE at K4/moderate/n50\"\n      convergence_at_n1000: \"<0.5% HB-MLE difference\"\n      rmse_penalty_k4_n50: \"up to 4.9×\"\n      rmse_penalty_k4_n100: \"up to 3.5×\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Budget sweep 是 double-edged sword for median tier。Positive：provides precise, actionable \n      crossover thresholds——reviewer 认为 this is good science。Negative：reveals that EC-HTE \n      operating window is restrictive。K=2/moderate: EC-HTE NEVER outperforms global on RMSE。\n      K=4/extreme: crossover at n=1000 (= 250 experts per subgroup)——expensive。K=4/moderate: \n      crossover at n=2000——impractical for most CSS studies。RMSE penalties at small n (up to \n      4.9×) 被 reviewer 视为 \"significant practical limitation, not just honest disclosure\" \n      (median core assumption #5)。W3 (Major) in review: \"the practical applicability window is \n      narrower than the paper's framing suggests.\" 这个实验 honest 但 directly undermines \n      excitement：reviewer 计算 \"for a typical CSS study with K=4 subgroups and moderate \n      heterogeneity, I need 2000 expert labels — that's a large-scale annotation project, \n      not a quick pilot.\" Abstract 的 \"as few as 250 expert labels\" technically correct \n      (K=2/extreme) but cherry-picks the best case。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: RMSE Crossover Points\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"Regime\", \"n_expert crossover\", \"Practical?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"2\", \"extreme\", \"250\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"2\", \"moderate\", \"never\", \"N/A — global always better\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"extreme\", \"1000\", \"Marginal\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"moderate\", \"2000\", \"Expensive\"]\n      - name: \"Table 7: RMSE Penalty at Small n_expert\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"n_expert\", \"RMSE ratio (EC-HTE / Global)\", \"Worst subgroup\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"2\", \"50\", \"1.8×\", \"z1\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"50\", \"4.9×\", \"D(π=0.30)\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"100\", \"3.5×\", \"D\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"250\", \"1.4×\", \"D\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"500\", \"1.1×\", \"all comparable\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 4: Budget crossover curves — RMSE ratio (EC-HTE/Global) vs n_expert for each (K, regime) combination. Shows EC-HTE only wins at large n for extreme heterogeneity.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reviewer 对 exp-006 的反应：appreciate the thoroughness but use the data against Claim 2。\n      \"EC-HTE is most valuable precisely when it is most needed\" 的 narrative 被 reviewer \n      接受 in principle，但 \"most needed\" (extreme heterogeneity) 和 \"affordable\" (n≤250) \n      的交集太小。W3 highlights that K=2/moderate NEVER crosses——meaning for the majority \n      of real-world scenarios (moderate heterogeneity is more common than extreme), global \n      correction is the right choice。This 是 Claim 2 acceptance rate 被压到 40-60% 的 key \n      evidence。Paper 的 defense 是 connecting to Claim 3 (diagnostic decides strategy)，\n      但 Claim 3 itself 在 setting level 不 work (exp-005)，所以 the chain breaks。\n\n  - name: \"PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      (a) PPCI vs EC-HTE on covariate vs outcome error; (b) per-subgroup DSL baseline; \n      (c) EC-HTE+PPCI composition for dual error; (d) pure covariate-error control condition.\n    expected_results:\n      total_rows: 6912\n      dgps: [\"A_covariate_only\", \"B_outcome_only\", \"C_both_errors\", \"D_no_error\"]\n      methods: 8\n      mc_runs: 100\n      dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias: 0.005\n      dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_rmse: 0.225\n      dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_bias: 0.178\n      dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_bias: 0.004\n      dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_rmse: 0.261\n      dgp_c_n500_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias: 0.005\n      dgp_c_n500_k2_ec_hte_ppci_rmse: 0.142\n      composition_bias_reduction_over_echte: \"35×\"\n      coverage_all_ppci_methods: 1.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      PPCI composition 是 paper 的 technical highlight——35× bias reduction in DGP C，near-zero \n      bias (0.005)。Median reviewer 对 composition result positive 但有两个 qualifications：\n      (1) PPCI alone (bias=0.004) achieves similar bias reduction in DGP C without EC-HTE—\n      reviewer 问 \"is EC-HTE really necessary here?\"。Paper 的 answer 是 PPCI has higher \n      RMSE (0.261 vs 0.225) 和 doesn't exploit CM structure——technically correct but the \n      advantage is modest。(2) Coverage=1.0 for all PPCI methods (W8 in review): \"Perfect \n      empirical coverage across 100 MC runs is statistically improbable under correct \n      calibration — this likely reflects inflated CIs.\" Over-conservative CIs 意味着 PPCI \n      methods 的 precision 很差。Reviewer 对 DSL comparison 接受——EC-HTE 的 partial pooling \n      advantage over per-subgroup DSL 是 valid。Overall：composition elevates Claim 4 但 \n      doesn't rescue Claims 2-3。DGP A (pure covariate error) 是 EC-HTE 的 strength case，\n      reviewer 认可。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: DGP C (Both Errors) — Key Results\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"|Bias| (z0)\", \"RMSE (z0)\", \"Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Naive\", \"0.251\", \"0.269\", \"0.85\"]\n          - [\"Global CM\", \"0.195\", \"0.238\", \"0.88\"]\n          - [\"EC-HTE\", \"0.178\", \"0.226\", \"0.92\"]\n          - [\"PPCI\", \"0.004\", \"0.261\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"EC-HTE+PPCI\", \"0.005\", \"0.225\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"Oracle (cov)\", \"0.180\", \"0.215\", \"0.93\"]\n      - name: \"Table 9: Cross-DGP Method Comparison (n=250, K=2, extreme)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"DGP A |Bias|\", \"DGP B |Bias|\", \"DGP C |Bias|\", \"DGP D |Bias|\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Naive\", \"0.12\", \"0.14\", \"0.25\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"Global\", \"0.08\", \"0.09\", \"0.20\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"EC-HTE\", \"0.01\", \"0.13\", \"0.18\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"PPCI\", \"0.03\", \"0.01\", \"0.004\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"EC-HTE+PPCI\", \"0.01\", \"0.01\", \"0.005\", \"0.001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Data presented in tables; no dedicated figure. Could benefit from a DGP comparison bar chart.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reviewer 对 PPCI composition 的评价：S5 (\"principled and effective\") 但视为 secondary \n      contribution。Key tension：在 DGP C 中 PPCI alone (bias=0.004) 几乎与 EC-HTE+PPCI \n      (0.005) 一样好——EC-HTE 的 marginal value 主要在 RMSE (0.261→0.225, 14% improvement)。\n      Reviewer 不认为这足以 justify EC-HTE 的 complexity。Coverage=1.0 被视为 red flag \n      (over-conservative CIs)——Q4 in review 直接问 CI width。This experiment supports \n      soundness 3.5-4.0 but contributes modestly to excitement。\n\n  - name: \"Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-3.5-turbo through GPT-5.4 (6 models, three generations): measure misclassification \n      heterogeneity patterns across models, show Δπ is structural not model-specific.\n    expected_results:\n      models_completed: 6\n      effective_delta_pi_range: \"0.08-0.198\"\n      all_delta_pi_above_005: true\n      worst_subgroup_consensus: \"True_medium (5/6 models)\"\n      spearman_significant_pairs: 4\n      filtered_subgroups: 4\n      excluded_subgroups: \"False_long (n=6), True_long (n=4)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-model analysis 是 paper 的 supporting evidence——confirms the premise (heterogeneous \n      misclassification is structural) rather than validating the solution。All 6 models \n      Δπ>0.05 和 5/6 sharing worst subgroup 是 clean result。但 Median reviewer notes：\n      (1) Δπ range 0.08-0.198——the lower end (GPT-4o: 0.08, GPT-4.1: 0.098) is moderate, \n      meaning most recent/best LLMs have modest heterogeneity where EC-HTE may not be needed \n      (K=2/moderate never crosses per exp-006)。(2) Only 4 effective subgroups after filtering \n      (excluded n<10 groups)——limited statistical power for rank correlation (most p>0.20)。\n      (3) All OpenAI models——no open-source model diversity。Reviewer 将 exp-008 视为 \n      \"nice supplement\" 放在 appendix appropriate，supports S6 (\"validates the premise\") \n      但不 move the needle on excitement。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 14 (Appendix A): Effective Δπ Across LLMs\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Generation\", \"Effective Δπ\", \"Worst Subgroup\", \"Overall Acc\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"gpt-3.5-turbo\", \"3.5\", \"0.198\", \"True_medium\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"gpt-4-turbo\", \"4\", \"0.149\", \"True_medium\", \"0.81\"]\n          - [\"gpt-4o\", \"4\", \"0.080\", \"True_medium\", \"0.84\"]\n          - [\"gpt-4o-mini\", \"4\", \"0.136\", \"True_medium\", \"0.79\"]\n          - [\"gpt-4.1\", \"4.1\", \"0.098\", \"True_medium\", \"0.86\"]\n          - [\"gpt-5.4\", \"5\", \"0.114\", \"True_medium\", \"0.88\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Appendix figure: bar chart of Δπ by model generation, showing heterogeneity persists but magnitude decreases with model capability.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reviewer 接受 exp-008 的 premise validation 但注意到 paradox：better LLMs have lower Δπ，\n      meaning the problem EC-HTE solves is becoming less severe as LLMs improve。GPT-5.4 \n      Δπ=0.114 vs GPT-3.5 Δπ=0.198——trend suggests the operating window is shrinking \n      over time。This doesn't invalidate the paper but dampens enthusiasm for long-term \n      impact。Appendix placement appropriate。\n\n  - name: \"Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      CATE-weighted allocation targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups, compare against \n      uniform and uncertainty-only allocation strategies.\n    expected_results:\n      allocation_strategies: 3\n      n_expert_total: 500\n      K: 4\n      cate_weighted_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform: \"8-12%\"\n      uncertainty_weighted_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform: \"3-5%\"\n      cate_weighted_coverage: 0.94\n      uniform_coverage: 0.93\n      practical_gain: \"modest\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Adaptive allocation 是 P2 experiment——appendix material。在 median tier 下 results \n      are positive but modest：8-12% RMSE improvement from CATE-weighted allocation vs \n      uniform。Reviewer 对此的反应是 \"interesting but tangential\"——allocation strategy \n      是 orthogonal to the core claims about bias identity and EC-HTE correction。Improvement \n      幅度不足以改变 paper 的 overall narrative。Reviewer 可能 note that adaptive allocation \n      requires knowing which subgroups have high CATE and high error a priori——circular \n      if you don't already have good subgroup estimates。不影响 overall score。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 15 (Appendix B): Allocation Strategy Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Strategy\", \"RMSE\", \"Coverage\", \"|Bias|\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Uniform\", \"0.108\", \"0.93\", \"0.012\"]\n          - [\"Uncertainty-weighted\", \"0.103\", \"0.93\", \"0.011\"]\n          - [\"CATE-weighted\", \"0.096\", \"0.94\", \"0.010\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"No figure; appendix table only.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix experiment，不影响 median tier scores。Reviewer 可能 skim 但 not cite in \n      review。Modest improvement (8-12%) 不足以成为 standalone contribution。在 revision \n      中可以 strengthen 或 drop without affecting outcome。\n\n  - name: \"Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      Test EC-HTE when subgroups are noisy/overlapping (0%, 10%, 25%, 50% noise levels). \n      Show graceful degradation of HB partial pooling under misspecification.\n    expected_results:\n      noise_levels: [0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5]\n      total_runs: 800\n      k2_coverage_hb_range: \"0.945-0.958\"\n      k2_coverage_naive_range: \"0.875-0.897\"\n      k2_coverage_global_range: \"0.925-0.945\"\n      k4_coverage_hb_range: \"0.946-0.960\"\n      hb_beats_mle_all_configs: true\n      graceful_convergence_at_50pct: true\n      hb_improvement_range: \"+0.1% to +0.9% RMSE\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Robustness analysis 是 positive result for paper——HB coverage 维持 94.5-96% across all \n      noise levels，graceful convergence toward global at 50% noise。Reviewer 对 robustness \n      analysis 的 reaction：appreciate the thoroughness (supports S4 in review) 但 note that \n      improvement over MLE is very modest (+0.1% to +0.9% RMSE)。The real story is coverage \n      stability——naive drops to 87.5% while HB stays above 94.5%。但 reviewer also notes \n      that this experiment tests synthetic noise injection, not real-world subgroup \n      misspecification——real misspecification (wrong subgroup variable entirely) would be \n      more severe。Appendix material, supports robustness claim without changing scores。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 16 (Appendix C): Coverage Under Subgroup Noise\"\n        columns: [\"Noise Level\", \"K\", \"Naive Cov\", \"Global Cov\", \"HB Cov\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0%\", \"2\", \"0.875\", \"0.925\", \"0.958\"]\n          - [\"10%\", \"2\", \"0.877\", \"0.935\", \"0.948\"]\n          - [\"25%\", \"2\", \"0.890\", \"0.932\", \"0.950\"]\n          - [\"50%\", \"2\", \"0.897\", \"0.945\", \"0.945\"]\n          - [\"0%\", \"4\", \"0.904\", \"0.930\", \"0.956\"]\n          - [\"25%\", \"4\", \"0.909\", \"0.948\", \"0.960\"]\n          - [\"50%\", \"4\", \"0.919\", \"0.944\", \"0.946\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"No main text figure; coverage vs noise level line plot in appendix.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Graceful degradation 是 expected result for HB shrinkage estimators——at maximum noise, \n      HB converges to global (by design)。Reviewer 不会对此 surprised 但 appreciate the \n      verification。Coverage as \"decisive metric\" 是 valid framing——naive 87-92% vs HB \n      95-96% is the strongest argument for EC-HTE in this experiment。但 improvement \n      is mainly in coverage (addressing undercoverage from ignoring heterogeneity), not \n      in point estimates。Supports Claim 2 at the margin。\n\n  - name: \"Causal Forest Integration\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      Apply EC-HTE post-hoc correction to CausalForestDML subgroup CATE estimates. Compare \n      naive, globally-corrected, and EC-HTE-corrected forests. K=2,4 × extreme/moderate × \n      n_expert=250,500.\n    expected_results:\n      n_mc: 100\n      n_configs: 8\n      total_rows: 144\n      runtime_min: 35\n      mean_abs_bias_naive_forest: 0.1558\n      mean_abs_bias_global_forest: 0.1073\n      mean_abs_bias_ec_hte_forest: 0.0608\n      mean_rmse_naive_forest: 0.1782\n      mean_rmse_global_forest: 0.1659\n      mean_rmse_ec_hte_forest: 0.2289\n      debiasing_hurts_cases: 9\n      debiasing_hurts_max_ratio: 5.9\n      k2_n500_ec_hte_bias_range: \"0.004-0.013\"\n      k2_n500_global_bias_range: \"0.033-0.109\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      CausalForest integration 是 paper 的 important validation——shows bias mechanism extends \n      beyond DIM to nonlinear CATE estimators，with amplification up to 5.9× (K=4/extreme) \n      vs 2.41× for DIM。EC-HTE achieves dramatic bias reduction (|bias|=0.06 vs naive 0.16, \n      62% reduction)。BUT the median-tier weakness is the RMSE tradeoff：EC-HTE RMSE 0.2289 \n      is 38% HIGHER than global 0.1659。Reviewer W4 (Moderate): \"EC-HTE reduces bias but \n      increases RMSE — by 38% for CausalForest. For practitioners, RMSE is often the primary \n      decision criterion.\" This experiment illustrates the fundamental bias-variance tradeoff \n      in EC-HTE：per-subgroup CM estimation reduces bias but introduces variance from small \n      expert samples。9 of 144 rows show debiasing-hurts (global worse than naive)——confirms \n      Claim 1 generalizes to CausalForest。K=2/n=500 is the sweet spot: ec_hte |bias|=0.004-0.013 \n      (near-zero) with manageable RMSE。But K=4/n=250 is the pain point：5.9× amplification \n      is dramatic 但 EC-HTE RMSE penalty equally dramatic。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: CausalForest Integration Results\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"Method\", \"|Bias|\", \"RMSE\", \"Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"K=2/extreme/n500\", \"Naive CF\", \"0.125\", \"0.143\", \"0.46\"]\n          - [\"K=2/extreme/n500\", \"Global CF\", \"0.104\", \"0.129\", \"0.65\"]\n          - [\"K=2/extreme/n500\", \"EC-HTE CF\", \"0.008\", \"0.082\", \"0.91\"]\n          - [\"K=4/extreme/n250\", \"Naive CF\", \"0.186\", \"0.202\", \"0.42\"]\n          - [\"K=4/extreme/n250\", \"Global CF\", \"0.098\", \"0.185\", \"0.58\"]\n          - [\"K=4/extreme/n250\", \"EC-HTE CF\", \"0.042\", \"0.285\", \"0.88\"]\n          - [\"Mean (all)\", \"Naive CF\", \"0.156\", \"0.178\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Mean (all)\", \"Global CF\", \"0.107\", \"0.166\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Mean (all)\", \"EC-HTE CF\", \"0.061\", \"0.229\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Data contributes to bias mechanism schematic (Figure 1) showing DIM vs CausalForest amplification patterns.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-011 的 dual signal 定义了 median tier 的 tension。Positive：5.9× amplification with \n      CausalForest is the paper's most dramatic result，EC-HTE bias reduction to near-zero \n      at K=2/n=500 is convincing。Negative：38% RMSE increase on average——reviewer asks \n      \"would a practitioner accept 38% worse total estimation quality for lower bias?\" The \n      answer depends on whether bias or RMSE is the relevant criterion，which depends on \n      the downstream use case。Paper doesn't provide guidance on this choice。Reviewer W4 \n      requests \"explicit bias-RMSE Pareto analysis showing when EC-HTE actually improves \n      total estimation quality versus when the variance cost outweighs the bias reduction.\" \n      This is the key revision request connecting exp-011 to the overall score。Coverage \n      improvement (naive 42-46% → EC-HTE 88-91%) is the strongest argument——undercoverage \n      leads to false discoveries in downstream inference。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14733,"cache_read_input_tokens":44077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14733},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4aab4440-3f1a-4989-8d2a-6845e346e8e8","uuid":"54a8332f-b030-460c-8af9-2aceed1c2432"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":314274,"duration_api_ms":315601,"num_turns":6,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Problem framing 有吸引力但 novelty perception 分裂：部分 reviewer 认为 'correction can hurt' \n  是 known intuition 的 formalization，EC-HTE 的 narrow operating regime 削弱 practical impact，\n  diagnostic 在 setting level 不 work。需要调整 claims 强度——Claim 1 降级为 'first formal \n  characterization of classical ME amplification in LLM annotation pipelines'，Claim 2 降级为 \n  'proof-of-concept correction demonstrating the identity is actionable'，Claim 3 承认 diagnostic \n  仅在 subgroup level 有效。补充实验方向：找一个 EC-HTE 在 real data 上 works 的案例。\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE on synthetic data: HB Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator \n      with partial pooling, compare against MLE/Laplace on full regime sweep (extreme/moderate/homogeneous \n      × n_expert 100-2000 × K=2,4 subgroups). 3600 MC runs.\n    expected_results:\n      mcmc_rhat_max: 1.024\n      mcmc_ess_min: 129\n      mcmc_divergent: 0\n      runtime_min: 69\n      total_mc_runs: 3600\n      hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50: \"4-9%\"\n      hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100: \"1-2%\"\n      hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate: \"6-9%\"\n      hb_coverage_min: 0.87\n      hb_coverage_median: 0.93\n      k4_extreme_n50_hb_rmse: 0.99\n      hyperprior_sensitivity_k2_rmse_variation: \"<1%\"\n      hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_rmse_variation: \"~4-5%\"\n      hyperprior_sensitivity_coverage_invariant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      HB partial pooling 在 synthetic DGP 上 works as expected——这是 James-Stein shrinkage 的\n      standard result，reviewer 不会对此感到 surprised。K=2 improvement 4-9% modest，K=4/extreme/n=50 \n      曾出现 singularity blowup（修复后 RMSE 从 509→0.27），但 reviewer 会将此视为 implementation \n      issue 而非 fundamental limitation。Coverage 0.87-0.93 reasonable 但未达 nominal 0.95。\n      Median reviewer 评价：technically sound (Soundness 3.5-4.0) 但 novelty 不高——HB Dirichlet \n      partial pooling 是 established technique (Gelman et al. BDA3)，improvement 幅度 modest，\n      且 hyperprior sensitivity at K=4 (~4-5%) 暗示 method 对 specification 有一定 sensitivity。\n      这个实验支持 Claim 2 的 technical validity 但不足以让 reviewer 认为 method 有 substantial \n      practical value。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=2)\"\n        columns: [\"n_expert\", \"Regime\", \"Subgroup\", \"MLE RMSE\", \"HB RMSE\", \"Δ%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"50\", \"extreme\", \"z0\", \"0.142\", \"0.131\", \"-7.7%\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"extreme\", \"z1\", \"0.156\", \"0.142\", \"-9.0%\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"moderate\", \"z0\", \"0.098\", \"0.094\", \"-4.1%\"]\n          - [\"100\", \"extreme\", \"z0\", \"0.095\", \"0.093\", \"-2.1%\"]\n          - [\"100\", \"extreme\", \"z1\", \"0.108\", \"0.107\", \"-0.9%\"]\n          - [\"250\", \"extreme\", \"z0\", \"0.068\", \"0.067\", \"-1.5%\"]\n          - [\"500\", \"extreme\", \"z0\", \"0.048\", \"0.048\", \"-0.0%\"]\n      - name: \"Table 4: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=4)\"\n        columns: [\"n_expert\", \"Regime\", \"Worst Subgroup\", \"MLE RMSE\", \"HB RMSE\", \"Δ%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"50\", \"extreme\", \"D(π=0.30)\", \"1.32\", \"0.99\", \"-25.0%\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"moderate\", \"C\", \"0.186\", \"0.170\", \"-8.6%\"]\n          - [\"100\", \"extreme\", \"D(π=0.30)\", \"0.38\", \"0.29\", \"-23.7%\"]\n          - [\"250\", \"extreme\", \"D\", \"0.135\", \"0.128\", \"-5.2%\"]\n          - [\"500\", \"all\", \"all\", \"~0.07\", \"~0.07\", \"<0.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"No figures from this experiment in main text; data feeds into budget crossover curves (Figure 4)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reviewer 对 exp-001 的反应分两极：measurement error / causal inference 背景的 reviewer \n      认为 HB Dirichlet-Multinomial partial pooling 是 textbook technique（BDA3 Ch. 5），\n      improvement 仅 4-9%（K=2）到 25%（K=4/extreme worst-case），不构成 methodological \n      contribution。NLP 背景 reviewer 可能认为 3600 MC runs 的 thoroughness 是 strength。\n      Coverage 0.87-0.93 是 concern——未达 nominal 95%，reviewer 会问 why。Hyperprior \n      sensitivity at K=4 (~4-5%) 被视为 acceptable 但需要 disclosure。Overall：支持 soundness \n      score 3.5-4.0，但不显著提升 excitement。\n\n  - name: \"Formal Bias Identity Verification\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      Derive bias = f(Δπ, Δτ) analytically, verify empirically across systematic parameter grid. \n      Produce 'debiasing can hurt' proposition with constructive two-subgroup example. K>2 extension.\n    expected_results:\n      r2_k2: 0.9939\n      r2_k4: 0.9738\n      tightness_ratio_k2_median: 1.0027\n      tightness_ratio_k4_median: 1.0234\n      debiasing_hurts_pct: 50\n      debiasing_hurts_threshold_delta_misclass: 0.1235\n      max_bias_ratio_k2: 2.86\n      max_bias_ratio_k4: 2.41\n      coverage_2se_k2: 0.951\n      coverage_2se_k4: 0.940\n      total_configs: 520\n    result_rationale: >\n      R²>0.97 confirms the identity is exact at population level——finite-sample MC noise 解释 \n      remaining variance。这是 paper 最强的 technical result：product form Bias ∝ Δπ×Δτ 是 exact \n      identity, not a bound。但 median reviewer 会有 novelty concern——至少一位 reviewer 有 \n      measurement error / causal inference 背景，认为这是 Fuller (1987) / Carroll (2006) 在 LLM \n      场景的 straightforward application。Qualitative insight \"correction can hurt when error is \n      heterogeneous\" 是 known (Fuller 1987, Sec 2.3: \"misspecified corrections amplify MSE\")。\n      Paper 的 contribution 是 (a) quantitative product form 和 (b) application to LLM annotation \n      pipelines。Debiasing hurts in 50% of parameter space 是 striking 但需要 qualification——\n      这 50% 包括所有 delta_misclass > 0.1235 的 configs，reviewer 问 \"how often does this \n      occur in practice?\"。Max amplification 2.86× (K=2) 和 2.41× (K=4) 的 non-monotonic \n      K-dependence 是 nuanced result，但 reviewer 可能 view this as \"moderate\" amplification \n      rather than \"dramatic\"。总体：claim1 被 75-90% reviewer 接受为 valid contribution，但 \n      perceived novelty 被 downweight 到 2.5-3.5 因为 formal novelty modest。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Bias Identity Verification (R²)\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"R²\", \"Tightness Ratio (median)\", \"Tightness Ratio (max)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"2\", \"0.994\", \"1.003\", \"1.021\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"0.974\", \"1.023\", \"1.089\"]\n      - name: \"Table 2: Debiasing Hurts Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"K=2\", \"K=4\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Configs where global hurts (%)\", \"50%\", \"50%\"]\n          - [\"Max bias amplification (DIM)\", \"2.86×\", \"2.41×\"]\n          - [\"Δπ threshold for hurt\", \"0.124\", \"0.124\"]\n          - [\"Coverage (2SE)\", \"0.951\", \"0.940\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: Δπ × Δτ bias amplification heatmap — color intensity shows bias ratio (global/naive), red region = debiasing hurts. Clear product-form structure visible.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 paper 的 theoretical backbone。Median reviewer 给 Soundness 3.5-4.0 因为 verification \n      thorough（520 configs, R²>0.97）。但 Excitement 因 novelty concern 被压到 3.0-3.5。\n      关键分歧点：NLP reviewer 可能认为 \"previously unrecognized bias mechanism\" 是 fair claim；\n      statistics reviewer 认为 qualitative insight is classical，quantitative form 只是 \n      routine derivation in a new application context。Paper 需要 explicitly acknowledge \n      Fuller/Carroll precedent 来 preempt 这个 objection（median framing 已 suggest \n      降级 claim wording）。50% hurt rate 和 2.86× max amplification 虽然 noteworthy \n      但不足以让 skeptical reviewer 升 excitement score——需要 real-data demonstration \n      that this actually matters。\n\n  - name: \"Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      Semi-synthetic benchmark using real CSS tweet corpus (TweetEval sentiment, N=45K). Inject \n      known CATE heterogeneity structure, annotate with GPT-4.1, apply EC-HTE vs baselines. \n      K=4 subgroups with misclass rates S0=0.05 to S3=0.25.\n    expected_results:\n      n_subgroups: 4\n      misclass_rates: \"S0=0.05, S1=0.10, S2=0.15, S3=0.25\"\n      delta_pi: 0.20\n      debiasing_hurts_confirmed: true\n      mc_runs: 100\n      hb_vs_mle_n50_S3_extreme_rmse_change: \"-57% (HB worse)\"\n      hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme_rmse_change: \"+60% (HB dramatically better)\"\n      hb_vs_mle_n250_S3_rmse_change: \"+5-17% (HB better)\"\n      hb_crossover: \"n_expert=100 per subgroup\"\n      boundary_condition: \"n_expert>=100 recommended; n=50 with extreme heterogeneity in tiny subgroups (12%) shows moderate degradation\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Semi-synthetic 设计 validates the bias identity in a more realistic setting——real text \n      corpus + injected CATE heterogeneity。Key finding: HB crossover at ~n=100 per subgroup \n      (≥25 experts/subgroup for 12% minority subgroups)。Reviewer 接受 semi-synthetic 作为 \n      valid evaluation framework 但注意到几个 concerns：(1) DGP 设计有 degrees of freedom——\n      misclass rates S0=0.05 to S3=0.25 创造了 ideal conditions for EC-HTE (Δπ=0.20 is \"extreme\")。\n      (2) n=50 boundary condition (HB worse by 57% at S3) 是 significant practical limitation——\n      K=4 with 12% minority means only 6 expert labels per subgroup，too few for reliable CM \n      estimation。(3) Semi-synthetic 不能 fully substitute for real-data validation。Reviewer \n      认为这个实验是 necessary but not sufficient for Claim 2。Pattern 与 exp-001 consistent，\n      支持 technical soundness。但 \"sweet spot is n=100-250\" 意味着 realistic expert budgets \n      are 400-1000 for K=4——reviewer 质疑 feasibility。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Semi-Synthetic EC-HTE Performance (K=4, extreme)\"\n        columns: [\"n_expert\", \"Method\", \"Subgroup\", \"|Bias|\", \"RMSE\", \"Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"50\", \"Naive\", \"S3(π=0.25)\", \"0.048\", \"0.109\", \"0.87\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"Global\", \"S3\", \"0.110\", \"0.140\", \"0.92\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"MLE\", \"S3\", \"0.085\", \"0.280\", \"0.90\"]\n          - [\"50\", \"HB\", \"S3\", \"0.072\", \"0.292\", \"0.93\"]\n          - [\"100\", \"HB\", \"S3\", \"0.018\", \"0.112\", \"0.94\"]\n          - [\"100\", \"Global\", \"S3\", \"0.105\", \"0.138\", \"0.92\"]\n          - [\"250\", \"HB\", \"S3\", \"0.009\", \"0.074\", \"0.95\"]\n          - [\"500\", \"HB\", \"all avg\", \"0.005\", \"0.052\", \"0.95\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Data feeds into Figure 4 (budget crossover curves)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Semi-synthetic 是 most controlled validation——reviewer 认为 technically sound 但 asks \n      \"how representative is this DGP?\" Δπ=0.20 是 extreme regime，而 exp-012 pilot 显示 \n      real GPT-4.1 的 Δπ=0.098 only (moderate)。这暗示 paper 的 headline numbers (near-zero \n      bias at n=250) 对应的是 favorable conditions，real-world performance 会 worse。Claim 2 \n      accepted as useful by 40-60%：technical validity 无争议，但 practical utility window \n      被认为 narrow。\n\n  - name: \"Real-Data Case Study (Pattern Consistency)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Apply EC-HTE to UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech corpus (N=2496). Show pattern consistency \n      with synthetic results. Framed as illustrative application, NOT ground-truth benchmark.\n    expected_results:\n      dataset: \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\"\n      n_comments: 2496\n      subgroups: 4\n      delta_pi: 0.117\n      global_FPR: 0.139\n      global_FNR: 0.533\n      avg_abs_bias_naive: 0.210\n      avg_abs_bias_global: 0.273\n      avg_abs_bias_ec_hte: 0.313\n      ec_hte_outperforms_global: false\n      cate_comparison: \"EC-HTE does not outperform global — high FNR (53%) and wide CIs limit correction effectiveness\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 median tier 的 critical weakness。EC-HTE avg |bias| 0.313 > global 0.273 > naive 0.210 \n      ——method 在 real data 上 makes things worse。Root cause：(1) global FNR=0.533 (LLM 严重 \n      under-classifies dehumanization)，近乎 random for positive class，CM inversion amplifies \n      noise；(2) Δπ=0.117 is moderate, not extreme；(3) subgroup-level expert labels insufficient。\n      Paper 将此 frame 为 \"operating condition mismatch\" 和 \"illustrative application\"，但 \n      reviewer 的反应是：这恰好是 the kind of real-world setting where practitioners would \n      apply the method。如果 method 仅在 carefully controlled synthetic conditions 下 work，\n      practical impact 严重受限。至少一位 reviewer 将此视为 major weakness，directly 影响 \n      Claim 2 acceptance rate (40-60%) 和 overall excitement (3.0-3.5)。Honest reporting \n      被 appreciated (S3 in review) 但不 mitigate the fundamental concern。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 12: Real-Data Case Study — UC Berkeley Hate Speech\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Avg |Bias|\", \"Subgroup Max |Bias|\", \"Mean CI Width\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Naive\", \"0.210\", \"0.35\", \"0.18\"]\n          - [\"Global Corrected\", \"0.273\", \"0.42\", \"0.22\"]\n          - [\"EC-HTE (HB)\", \"0.313\", \"0.51\", \"0.34\"]\n      - name: \"Table 13: Subgroup Misclassification Rates\"\n        columns: [\"Subgroup\", \"FPR\", \"FNR\", \"Overall Error\", \"n\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"plat0_long\", \"0.064\", \"0.468\", \"0.266\", \"624\"]\n          - [\"plat0_short\", \"0.101\", \"0.573\", \"0.337\", \"624\"]\n          - [\"plat23_long\", \"0.077\", \"0.530\", \"0.303\", \"624\"]\n          - [\"plat23_short\", \"0.139\", \"0.627\", \"0.383\", \"624\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"No figure; results presented as tables only. Reviewer W5 notes absence of figures as presentation weakness.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-004 是 median tier 最被 reviewer 攻击的实验。W2 (Major) in review: \"EC-HTE's average \n      absolute bias (0.313) is worse than both naive (0.210) and global corrected (0.273).\" \n      Paper 的 defense (\"operating condition mismatch\") 在逻辑上成立（FNR=53% violates \n      practical CM invertibility），但 reviewer 反问：\"how often do real datasets satisfy \n      the conditions?\" 这直接压低 Claim 2 acceptance 到 40-60%。exp-015/016 的 negative \n      results 进一步 confirm：neither low-FNR (gpt-3.5) nor low-FPR (GPT-4.1) real CMs \n      enable EC-HTE to beat global when P(Z=1)=0.18。Median reviewer 接受 honest disclosure \n      但给 excitement 3.0——\"the method fails outside carefully controlled synthetic conditions.\"\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Criterion Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Compute Δπ × Δτ product from pilot data across all settings. ROC analysis of threshold \n      for predicting when global correction fails. Cross-validated evaluation.\n    expected_results:\n      subgroup_level_auc: 0.833\n      subgroup_level_correlation: 0.86\n      setting_level_auc: 0.49\n      low_pi_hurt_pct: 84.6\n      high_pi_hurt_pct: 15.4\n      theory_alignment: \"consistent with exp-002 formula\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Setting-level AUC=0.49 是 median tier 的 second critical weakness。Diagnostic 在 practitioner \n      实际需要做决策的 granularity（\"should I use EC-HTE for this analysis?\"）上 no better than \n      random。Subgroup-level AUC=0.833 表面上 impressive，但 reviewer 指出两个问题：(1) subgroup-level \n      decision 需要已知 subgroup structure，而 knowing which subgroups exist 本身就需要 domain \n      knowledge——循环论证；(2) AUC 0.833 with ~15% false positive rate means 1 in 7 flagged \n      subgroups is false alarm。Claim 3 accepted by only 30-50% of reviewers。Paper 的 reframe \n      (\"two-stage decision workflow: flag subgroups → consult budget\") partially mitigates but \n      doesn't resolve the fundamental gap。Reviewer 建议 explore alternative diagnostic statistics \n      or acknowledge diagnostic is subgroup-level only。This experiment 直接决定了 Claim 3 的 fate \n      in median tier。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Diagnostic Criterion Performance\"\n        columns: [\"Level\", \"AUC\", \"Correlation\", \"Precision@0.5\", \"Recall@0.5\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Subgroup-level\", \"0.833\", \"0.86\", \"0.78\", \"0.85\"]\n          - [\"Setting-level (CV)\", \"0.49\", \"0.12\", \"0.51\", \"0.48\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3: Subgroup-level ROC curve for Δπ×Δτ diagnostic. Shows reasonable discrimination at subgroup level (AUC=0.83) but would need separate panel showing setting-level failure (AUC=0.49) for honest presentation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-005 的 split result 是 median tier 的 defining feature。Strong subgroup AUC + failed \n      setting AUC creates a narrative tension：the diagnostic works where you already know the \n      answer (subgroup level) but fails where you need it most (setting level)。Reviewer W1 (Major): \n      \"Contribution 3 in the introduction leads with 'AUC=0.83' without immediately clarifying \n      this is subgroup-level only — this creates a misleading first impression.\" Paper 需要 \n      reframe Claim 3 更 carefully——lead with setting-level failure, then present subgroup-level \n      as partial recovery。This is the key revision request for median tier.\n\n  - name: \"Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Systematic sweep n_expert ∈ {50, 100, 250, 500, 1000, 2000} × K ∈ {2, 4} × regime. \n      Find crossover point where EC-HTE > Global on RMSE. Validate HB partial pooling value.\n    expected_results:\n      total_rows: 288\n      runtime_min: 110\n      crossover_K2_extreme: 250\n      crossover_K2_moderate: \"never\"\n      crossover_K4_extreme: 1000\n      crossover_K4_moderate: 2000\n      hb_vs_mle_win_rate: \"21/24 (87.5%)\"\n      hb_best_improvement_over_mle: \"+42.4% RMSE at K4/moderate/n50\"\n      convergence_at_n1000: \"<0.5% HB-MLE difference\"\n      rmse_penalty_k4_n50: \"up to 4.9×\"\n      rmse_penalty_k4_n100: \"up to 3.5×\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Budget sweep 是 double-edged sword for median tier。Positive：provides precise, actionable \n      crossover thresholds——reviewer 认为 this is good science。Negative：reveals that EC-HTE \n      operating window is restrictive。K=2/moderate: EC-HTE NEVER outperforms global on RMSE。\n      K=4/extreme: crossover at n=1000 (= 250 experts per subgroup)——expensive。K=4/moderate: \n      crossover at n=2000——impractical for most CSS studies。RMSE penalties at small n (up to \n      4.9×) 被 reviewer 视为 \"significant practical limitation, not just honest disclosure\" \n      (median core assumption #5)。W3 (Major) in review: \"the practical applicability window is \n      narrower than the paper's framing suggests.\" 这个实验 honest 但 directly undermines \n      excitement：reviewer 计算 \"for a typical CSS study with K=4 subgroups and moderate \n      heterogeneity, I need 2000 expert labels — that's a large-scale annotation project, \n      not a quick pilot.\" Abstract 的 \"as few as 250 expert labels\" technically correct \n      (K=2/extreme) but cherry-picks the best case。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: RMSE Crossover Points\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"Regime\", \"n_expert crossover\", \"Practical?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"2\", \"extreme\", \"250\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"2\", \"moderate\", \"never\", \"N/A — global always better\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"extreme\", \"1000\", \"Marginal\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"moderate\", \"2000\", \"Expensive\"]\n      - name: \"Table 7: RMSE Penalty at Small n_expert\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"n_expert\", \"RMSE ratio (EC-HTE / Global)\", \"Worst subgroup\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"2\", \"50\", \"1.8×\", \"z1\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"50\", \"4.9×\", \"D(π=0.30)\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"100\", \"3.5×\", \"D\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"250\", \"1.4×\", \"D\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"500\", \"1.1×\", \"all comparable\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 4: Budget crossover curves — RMSE ratio (EC-HTE/Global) vs n_expert for each (K, regime) combination. Shows EC-HTE only wins at large n for extreme heterogeneity.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reviewer 对 exp-006 的反应：appreciate the thoroughness but use the data against Claim 2。\n      \"EC-HTE is most valuable precisely when it is most needed\" 的 narrative 被 reviewer \n      接受 in principle，但 \"most needed\" (extreme heterogeneity) 和 \"affordable\" (n≤250) \n      的交集太小。W3 highlights that K=2/moderate NEVER crosses——meaning for the majority \n      of real-world scenarios (moderate heterogeneity is more common than extreme), global \n      correction is the right choice。This 是 Claim 2 acceptance rate 被压到 40-60% 的 key \n      evidence。Paper 的 defense 是 connecting to Claim 3 (diagnostic decides strategy)，\n      但 Claim 3 itself 在 setting level 不 work (exp-005)，所以 the chain breaks。\n\n  - name: \"PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      (a) PPCI vs EC-HTE on covariate vs outcome error; (b) per-subgroup DSL baseline; \n      (c) EC-HTE+PPCI composition for dual error; (d) pure covariate-error control condition.\n    expected_results:\n      total_rows: 6912\n      dgps: [\"A_covariate_only\", \"B_outcome_only\", \"C_both_errors\", \"D_no_error\"]\n      methods: 8\n      mc_runs: 100\n      dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias: 0.005\n      dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_rmse: 0.225\n      dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_bias: 0.178\n      dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_bias: 0.004\n      dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_rmse: 0.261\n      dgp_c_n500_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias: 0.005\n      dgp_c_n500_k2_ec_hte_ppci_rmse: 0.142\n      composition_bias_reduction_over_echte: \"35×\"\n      coverage_all_ppci_methods: 1.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      PPCI composition 是 paper 的 technical highlight——35× bias reduction in DGP C，near-zero \n      bias (0.005)。Median reviewer 对 composition result positive 但有两个 qualifications：\n      (1) PPCI alone (bias=0.004) achieves similar bias reduction in DGP C without EC-HTE—\n      reviewer 问 \"is EC-HTE really necessary here?\"。Paper 的 answer 是 PPCI has higher \n      RMSE (0.261 vs 0.225) 和 doesn't exploit CM structure——technically correct but the \n      advantage is modest。(2) Coverage=1.0 for all PPCI methods (W8 in review): \"Perfect \n      empirical coverage across 100 MC runs is statistically improbable under correct \n      calibration — this likely reflects inflated CIs.\" Over-conservative CIs 意味着 PPCI \n      methods 的 precision 很差。Reviewer 对 DSL comparison 接受——EC-HTE 的 partial pooling \n      advantage over per-subgroup DSL 是 valid。Overall：composition elevates Claim 4 但 \n      doesn't rescue Claims 2-3。DGP A (pure covariate error) 是 EC-HTE 的 strength case，\n      reviewer 认可。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: DGP C (Both Errors) — Key Results\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"|Bias| (z0)\", \"RMSE (z0)\", \"Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Naive\", \"0.251\", \"0.269\", \"0.85\"]\n          - [\"Global CM\", \"0.195\", \"0.238\", \"0.88\"]\n          - [\"EC-HTE\", \"0.178\", \"0.226\", \"0.92\"]\n          - [\"PPCI\", \"0.004\", \"0.261\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"EC-HTE+PPCI\", \"0.005\", \"0.225\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"Oracle (cov)\", \"0.180\", \"0.215\", \"0.93\"]\n      - name: \"Table 9: Cross-DGP Method Comparison (n=250, K=2, extreme)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"DGP A |Bias|\", \"DGP B |Bias|\", \"DGP C |Bias|\", \"DGP D |Bias|\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Naive\", \"0.12\", \"0.14\", \"0.25\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"Global\", \"0.08\", \"0.09\", \"0.20\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"EC-HTE\", \"0.01\", \"0.13\", \"0.18\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"PPCI\", \"0.03\", \"0.01\", \"0.004\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"EC-HTE+PPCI\", \"0.01\", \"0.01\", \"0.005\", \"0.001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Data presented in tables; no dedicated figure. Could benefit from a DGP comparison bar chart.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reviewer 对 PPCI composition 的评价：S5 (\"principled and effective\") 但视为 secondary \n      contribution。Key tension：在 DGP C 中 PPCI alone (bias=0.004) 几乎与 EC-HTE+PPCI \n      (0.005) 一样好——EC-HTE 的 marginal value 主要在 RMSE (0.261→0.225, 14% improvement)。\n      Reviewer 不认为这足以 justify EC-HTE 的 complexity。Coverage=1.0 被视为 red flag \n      (over-conservative CIs)——Q4 in review 直接问 CI width。This experiment supports \n      soundness 3.5-4.0 but contributes modestly to excitement。\n\n  - name: \"Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-3.5-turbo through GPT-5.4 (6 models, three generations): measure misclassification \n      heterogeneity patterns across models, show Δπ is structural not model-specific.\n    expected_results:\n      models_completed: 6\n      effective_delta_pi_range: \"0.08-0.198\"\n      all_delta_pi_above_005: true\n      worst_subgroup_consensus: \"True_medium (5/6 models)\"\n      spearman_significant_pairs: 4\n      filtered_subgroups: 4\n      excluded_subgroups: \"False_long (n=6), True_long (n=4)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-model analysis 是 paper 的 supporting evidence——confirms the premise (heterogeneous \n      misclassification is structural) rather than validating the solution。All 6 models \n      Δπ>0.05 和 5/6 sharing worst subgroup 是 clean result。但 Median reviewer notes：\n      (1) Δπ range 0.08-0.198——the lower end (GPT-4o: 0.08, GPT-4.1: 0.098) is moderate, \n      meaning most recent/best LLMs have modest heterogeneity where EC-HTE may not be needed \n      (K=2/moderate never crosses per exp-006)。(2) Only 4 effective subgroups after filtering \n      (excluded n<10 groups)——limited statistical power for rank correlation (most p>0.20)。\n      (3) All OpenAI models——no open-source model diversity。Reviewer 将 exp-008 视为 \n      \"nice supplement\" 放在 appendix appropriate，supports S6 (\"validates the premise\") \n      但不 move the needle on excitement。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 14 (Appendix A): Effective Δπ Across LLMs\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Generation\", \"Effective Δπ\", \"Worst Subgroup\", \"Overall Acc\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"gpt-3.5-turbo\", \"3.5\", \"0.198\", \"True_medium\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"gpt-4-turbo\", \"4\", \"0.149\", \"True_medium\", \"0.81\"]\n          - [\"gpt-4o\", \"4\", \"0.080\", \"True_medium\", \"0.84\"]\n          - [\"gpt-4o-mini\", \"4\", \"0.136\", \"True_medium\", \"0.79\"]\n          - [\"gpt-4.1\", \"4.1\", \"0.098\", \"True_medium\", \"0.86\"]\n          - [\"gpt-5.4\", \"5\", \"0.114\", \"True_medium\", \"0.88\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Appendix figure: bar chart of Δπ by model generation, showing heterogeneity persists but magnitude decreases with model capability.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reviewer 接受 exp-008 的 premise validation 但注意到 paradox：better LLMs have lower Δπ，\n      meaning the problem EC-HTE solves is becoming less severe as LLMs improve。GPT-5.4 \n      Δπ=0.114 vs GPT-3.5 Δπ=0.198——trend suggests the operating window is shrinking \n      over time。This doesn't invalidate the paper but dampens enthusiasm for long-term \n      impact。Appendix placement appropriate。\n\n  - name: \"Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      CATE-weighted allocation targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups, compare against \n      uniform and uncertainty-only allocation strategies.\n    expected_results:\n      allocation_strategies: 3\n      n_expert_total: 500\n      K: 4\n      cate_weighted_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform: \"8-12%\"\n      uncertainty_weighted_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform: \"3-5%\"\n      cate_weighted_coverage: 0.94\n      uniform_coverage: 0.93\n      practical_gain: \"modest\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Adaptive allocation 是 P2 experiment——appendix material。在 median tier 下 results \n      are positive but modest：8-12% RMSE improvement from CATE-weighted allocation vs \n      uniform。Reviewer 对此的反应是 \"interesting but tangential\"——allocation strategy \n      是 orthogonal to the core claims about bias identity and EC-HTE correction。Improvement \n      幅度不足以改变 paper 的 overall narrative。Reviewer 可能 note that adaptive allocation \n      requires knowing which subgroups have high CATE and high error a priori——circular \n      if you don't already have good subgroup estimates。不影响 overall score。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 15 (Appendix B): Allocation Strategy Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Strategy\", \"RMSE\", \"Coverage\", \"|Bias|\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Uniform\", \"0.108\", \"0.93\", \"0.012\"]\n          - [\"Uncertainty-weighted\", \"0.103\", \"0.93\", \"0.011\"]\n          - [\"CATE-weighted\", \"0.096\", \"0.94\", \"0.010\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"No figure; appendix table only.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix experiment，不影响 median tier scores。Reviewer 可能 skim 但 not cite in \n      review。Modest improvement (8-12%) 不足以成为 standalone contribution。在 revision \n      中可以 strengthen 或 drop without affecting outcome。\n\n  - name: \"Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      Test EC-HTE when subgroups are noisy/overlapping (0%, 10%, 25%, 50% noise levels). \n      Show graceful degradation of HB partial pooling under misspecification.\n    expected_results:\n      noise_levels: [0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5]\n      total_runs: 800\n      k2_coverage_hb_range: \"0.945-0.958\"\n      k2_coverage_naive_range: \"0.875-0.897\"\n      k2_coverage_global_range: \"0.925-0.945\"\n      k4_coverage_hb_range: \"0.946-0.960\"\n      hb_beats_mle_all_configs: true\n      graceful_convergence_at_50pct: true\n      hb_improvement_range: \"+0.1% to +0.9% RMSE\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Robustness analysis 是 positive result for paper——HB coverage 维持 94.5-96% across all \n      noise levels，graceful convergence toward global at 50% noise。Reviewer 对 robustness \n      analysis 的 reaction：appreciate the thoroughness (supports S4 in review) 但 note that \n      improvement over MLE is very modest (+0.1% to +0.9% RMSE)。The real story is coverage \n      stability——naive drops to 87.5% while HB stays above 94.5%。但 reviewer also notes \n      that this experiment tests synthetic noise injection, not real-world subgroup \n      misspecification——real misspecification (wrong subgroup variable entirely) would be \n      more severe。Appendix material, supports robustness claim without changing scores。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 16 (Appendix C): Coverage Under Subgroup Noise\"\n        columns: [\"Noise Level\", \"K\", \"Naive Cov\", \"Global Cov\", \"HB Cov\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0%\", \"2\", \"0.875\", \"0.925\", \"0.958\"]\n          - [\"10%\", \"2\", \"0.877\", \"0.935\", \"0.948\"]\n          - [\"25%\", \"2\", \"0.890\", \"0.932\", \"0.950\"]\n          - [\"50%\", \"2\", \"0.897\", \"0.945\", \"0.945\"]\n          - [\"0%\", \"4\", \"0.904\", \"0.930\", \"0.956\"]\n          - [\"25%\", \"4\", \"0.909\", \"0.948\", \"0.960\"]\n          - [\"50%\", \"4\", \"0.919\", \"0.944\", \"0.946\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"No main text figure; coverage vs noise level line plot in appendix.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Graceful degradation 是 expected result for HB shrinkage estimators——at maximum noise, \n      HB converges to global (by design)。Reviewer 不会对此 surprised 但 appreciate the \n      verification。Coverage as \"decisive metric\" 是 valid framing——naive 87-92% vs HB \n      95-96% is the strongest argument for EC-HTE in this experiment。但 improvement \n      is mainly in coverage (addressing undercoverage from ignoring heterogeneity), not \n      in point estimates。Supports Claim 2 at the margin。\n\n  - name: \"Causal Forest Integration\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      Apply EC-HTE post-hoc correction to CausalForestDML subgroup CATE estimates. Compare \n      naive, globally-corrected, and EC-HTE-corrected forests. K=2,4 × extreme/moderate × \n      n_expert=250,500.\n    expected_results:\n      n_mc: 100\n      n_configs: 8\n      total_rows: 144\n      runtime_min: 35\n      mean_abs_bias_naive_forest: 0.1558\n      mean_abs_bias_global_forest: 0.1073\n      mean_abs_bias_ec_hte_forest: 0.0608\n      mean_rmse_naive_forest: 0.1782\n      mean_rmse_global_forest: 0.1659\n      mean_rmse_ec_hte_forest: 0.2289\n      debiasing_hurts_cases: 9\n      debiasing_hurts_max_ratio: 5.9\n      k2_n500_ec_hte_bias_range: \"0.004-0.013\"\n      k2_n500_global_bias_range: \"0.033-0.109\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      CausalForest integration 是 paper 的 important validation——shows bias mechanism extends \n      beyond DIM to nonlinear CATE estimators，with amplification up to 5.9× (K=4/extreme) \n      vs 2.41× for DIM。EC-HTE achieves dramatic bias reduction (|bias|=0.06 vs naive 0.16, \n      62% reduction)。BUT the median-tier weakness is the RMSE tradeoff：EC-HTE RMSE 0.2289 \n      is 38% HIGHER than global 0.1659。Reviewer W4 (Moderate): \"EC-HTE reduces bias but \n      increases RMSE — by 38% for CausalForest. For practitioners, RMSE is often the primary \n      decision criterion.\" This experiment illustrates the fundamental bias-variance tradeoff \n      in EC-HTE：per-subgroup CM estimation reduces bias but introduces variance from small \n      expert samples。9 of 144 rows show debiasing-hurts (global worse than naive)——confirms \n      Claim 1 generalizes to CausalForest。K=2/n=500 is the sweet spot: ec_hte |bias|=0.004-0.013 \n      (near-zero) with manageable RMSE。But K=4/n=250 is the pain point：5.9× amplification \n      is dramatic 但 EC-HTE RMSE penalty equally dramatic。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: CausalForest Integration Results\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"Method\", \"|Bias|\", \"RMSE\", \"Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"K=2/extreme/n500\", \"Naive CF\", \"0.125\", \"0.143\", \"0.46\"]\n          - [\"K=2/extreme/n500\", \"Global CF\", \"0.104\", \"0.129\", \"0.65\"]\n          - [\"K=2/extreme/n500\", \"EC-HTE CF\", \"0.008\", \"0.082\", \"0.91\"]\n          - [\"K=4/extreme/n250\", \"Naive CF\", \"0.186\", \"0.202\", \"0.42\"]\n          - [\"K=4/extreme/n250\", \"Global CF\", \"0.098\", \"0.185\", \"0.58\"]\n          - [\"K=4/extreme/n250\", \"EC-HTE CF\", \"0.042\", \"0.285\", \"0.88\"]\n          - [\"Mean (all)\", \"Naive CF\", \"0.156\", \"0.178\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Mean (all)\", \"Global CF\", \"0.107\", \"0.166\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Mean (all)\", \"EC-HTE CF\", \"0.061\", \"0.229\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Data contributes to bias mechanism schematic (Figure 1) showing DIM vs CausalForest amplification patterns.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-011 的 dual signal 定义了 median tier 的 tension。Positive：5.9× amplification with \n      CausalForest is the paper's most dramatic result，EC-HTE bias reduction to near-zero \n      at K=2/n=500 is convincing。Negative：38% RMSE increase on average——reviewer asks \n      \"would a practitioner accept 38% worse total estimation quality for lower bias?\" The \n      answer depends on whether bias or RMSE is the relevant criterion，which depends on \n      the downstream use case。Paper doesn't provide guidance on this choice。Reviewer W4 \n      requests \"explicit bias-RMSE Pareto analysis showing when EC-HTE actually improves \n      total estimation quality versus when the variance cost outweighs the bias reduction.\" \n      This is the key revision request connecting exp-011 to the overall score。Coverage \n      improvement (naive 42-46% → EC-HTE 88-91%) is the strongest argument——undercoverage \n      leads to false discoveries in downstream inference。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4aab4440-3f1a-4989-8d2a-6845e346e8e8","total_cost_usd":0.7632477499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46969,"cache_read_input_tokens":177675,"output_tokens":14312,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46969,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":12813,"cache_read_input_tokens":44077,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14733},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":22874,"outputTokens":30,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.023024,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":6,"outputTokens":14312,"cacheReadInputTokens":177675,"cacheCreationInputTokens":46969,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.74022375,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"fbf3c2d0-c26a-4cf5-8428-a5faf0f0d302"}
